  {"id":"cuw.factory.inline-gateway-selection-before-selected-Execute","source":"CUW.dll","rvas":["0x59f75","0x5a920","0x5add0"],"matrix":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","inputs":{"worker+0xbd4":"operationmode: branch requires1","worker+0xc45":"suppresses fresh gateway mode changes whennonzero","mastercolumn":"FlagToChangeToReprogGWModeForCentralGW","masterkeys":"KindOfECU,firstCPUType,ContactType; never guessed from display label"},"ordered_branches":["Before phase/legacy Execute, querymaster FlagToCancelAutomaticIGOFF into initializedfalse local; queryfailure throwsint32(2). Ifworker+0xc45!=0 forcefalse. Otherwise Phase6 exactcontact plus selectednode imported Ethernetprotocol literal forcestrue.","For mode1 with automatic-IGOFF cancellation flagtrue, invokeCUW0x5add0 first. ExactContactType comparisons against native literals1007a600 and1007a62c gate SwitchConnection(6) before inlinehelper0x1a400; then restoreSwitchConnection(3) for equalitywithliteral1007a600, orSwitchConnection(0x8013) for equalitywithliteral1007a62c(Ethernet). Othercontacts callinlinehelper without those connection switches. No protocol inferred from contact displaytext; literal1007a600 is retained by exactsourceaddress rather than an unobservedlabel. Inline wire semantics remainFlashLegacy.","Next querymaster FlagToChangeToReprogGWModeForCentralGW into initializedfalse local; queryfailure throwsint32(2). Ifworker+0xc45!=0 forcefalse and skip fresh helper.","When centralGWflagtrue andmode1 andnot suppressed: worker+0xbe4=0 and publishrecovery1008dbf8=0; callCUW0x5a920(worker,outAttempted). That wrapper calls inlineCUW0x1af50(J2534=*(worker+0x44),callbacks=worker+0x88), copiesglobal1008ae48 lowbyte toworker+0xbfd, setsoutAttempted1 andreturnstrue on normal path. Callertrue setsworker+0xbe4=1,recovery1008dbf8=1.","If centralGWcondition false, nofresh inlinecentralGWhelper; resume-armed andnotdisabled recovers gateway/repro flags instead.","Only after those gates does caller choose phaseExecute vslegacyExecute via earlier selectorBH. Thus gateway inlinehelper mayprecede either selectedengine; never infer protocol/legacy algorithm owner from configured DLLname orContactType text."],"ownership":"Exact selection/ABI joins only; all helper request/wire algorithms remainFlashLegacy, transport switchmechanics remainFlashTransport/Drivers.","contract_id":"cuw.factory.inline-gateway-selection-before-selected-Execute","component":"factories","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.core"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.execute","rva":"0xb3e0","abi":{"export_rva":"0x1073","calling_convention":"x86 cdecl","inputs":["const typCallBacks* callbacks","typData* context"],"result":"bool in AL; caller clears 8 bytes of arguments"},"ordered_behavior":["Store callbacks at global RVA174f0 and context at174f4. Import CJ2534IF from context+0x54, then CalibrationFile from context base.","Initial phase context+0x978==0 calls CID engine0x6f20. Otherwise exact ContactType comparisons to imported glptrContactType_P5_Unified, glptrContactType_Phase6, glptrContactType_Ethernet select node route; all other values select classic route. These are complete NUL-terminated byte-string comparisons, not substring tests or inferred protocols.","Classic route reads CpuLoopBetweenPrepareAndWriteFlag from parameter[currentCPU]. Bool is initialized false; accessor return ignored. False gives outer end=currentCPU+1; true gives end=GetNumCPUImages(). Iterate from captured currentCPU. Set per-iteration result=true; independently test current phase==1 then call classic_prepare, phase==3 then call gateway_mode(result), phase==2 then classic_write. These are independent if statements: one Execute may perform prepare -> gateway -> write without returning.","Break on false. Before another outer CPU iteration, callback+0x4c(ctx,kind,CPU(next),contact,\"FlagToDoIGOFFONAtCPUTypeChange\",bool*) decides whether to stop; default false. If not stopped set phase=1. The outer loop uses a local index and does not itself assign context+0x738.","After classic route only, if global DH flag174fc is true AND result true AND current phase==2, allocate CanDiagCommUtils8 and DHUtils28, call DHUtils vslot+8 with1020(0x3fc), suppress any exception from that call, free both allocations using sized delete, clear DH flag. Keep original success result even if DH cleanup throws.","Node route only independently tests phase==1 ->node_prepare then phase==2 ->node_write. Initial phase3 on this route has no handler and returns false.","On every ordinary completion, export CJ2534IF first to context+0x54, then CalibrationFile to context base; return result. No mutex or per-invocation storage isolation: globals make concurrent/reentrant calls unsafe. Exceptions outside local catches are not converted into generic success."],"joins":["FlashTransport.CJ2534IF.ImportData/ExportData","FlashShared.CalibrationFile.ImportData/ExportData","FlashShared.CDHUtils.vslot8"],"instruction_pins":["0x1000b3e0..0x1000b42b stores/imports/phase0 gate","0x1000b475..0x1000b4f9 exact contact branches","0x1000b51f GetParameterbool","0x1000b6e9 ff5008 DH cleanup","0x1000b74a call export;0x1000b74f mov al,bl;0x1000b762 ret"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.execute","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.disconnect","rva":"0xb3d0","abi":{"export_rva":"0x10cd","calling_convention":"x86 cdecl, no arguments","result":"void"},"ordered_behavior":["MOV ECX,global CJ2534IF address100175b8; tail-JMP imported virtual Disconnect. Does not import/export context, clear phase, free loaded writer, or clear DH flag. Exceptions follow callee behavior."],"joins":["FlashTransport.CJ2534IF.Disconnect"],"instruction_pins":["0x1000b3d0 b9b8750110","0x1000b3d5 ff2544820110"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.disconnect","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.periodic_query","rva":"0xb850","abi":{"export_rva":"0x1181","calling_convention":"x86 cdecl, no arguments","result":"bool in AL, inherited from imported decorated QAE_NXZ method; Ghidra void is incorrect"},"ordered_behavior":["Set ECX=100175b8 and tail-JMP IsSendingSyncPeriodicMsg. Pure forwarding; no phase/import/export logic."],"joins":["FlashTransport.CJ2534IF.IsSendingSyncPeriodicMsg"],"instruction_pins":["0x1000b850 b9b8750110","0x1000b855 ff254c820110"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.periodic_query","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.dh_gateway","rva":"0xb280","abi":{"export_rva":"0x125d","calling_convention":"x86 cdecl","inputs":["const typCallBacks* callbacks","CJ2534IF* device","bool* changed_out"],"result":"void; writes changed_out on successful method path"},"ordered_behavior":["Construct CanDiagCommUtils(callbacks,device), then DHUtils(callbacks,device,global parameterArray,canUtils). Call DHUtils vslot0 with1020. Query IsDHCentralGWModeCouldBeChanged; save AL to global174fc and to changed_out. Free canUtils first then dhUtils using sized delete8/28.","Catch-all around DH operation frees both then rethrows via _CxxThrowException(NULL,NULL); do not replace with false success. Allocation/constructor unwind follows C++ EH state. There is no graceful null-allocation fallback: decompiled null branches still reach virtual dereference.","No packet bytes or gateway request payload are constructed by this module; vslot0 behavior and packet definitions belong to FlashShared.CDHUtils."],"joins":["FlashShared.CCanDiagCommUtils.constructor","FlashShared.CDHUtils.constructor/vslot0/IsDHCentralGWModeCouldBeChanged"],"instruction_pins":["0x1000b328 ff10","0x1000b32c call[100181d0]","0x1000b337 a2fc740110","0x1000b33d 8801","0x1000b361 catch frees then rethrows"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.dh_gateway","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.cid","rva":"0x6f20","abi":{"inputs":["global callbacks/context/J2534IF/CalibrationFile/parameterArray"],"result":"bool supplied through plugin out-bool"},"ordered_behavior":["Build parameter filename KindOfECU+ContactType+ProtocolAtNode(0 if any node, otherwise empty)+CPUType(0)+\".ini\" without delimiters. LoadParameter(parameter[0],filename,NULL), then SetKeys(kind,CPU0,contact+protocol). Either false throws CPassThruException9999.","Get GetCANIDFunctionNameForGetCID into zeroed260-byte buffer. If nonempty construct CCommunicationAddress(parameter0,callbacks,calibration), resolve a vector containing that function with no CID/location input; false resolution throws9999. Address record storage stride7 bytes.","Get DLLFileNameForGetCID; copy NUL-terminated path to context+0x764. Get file-version string to context+0x863, then require version_gate. LoadLibraryA and require StartGetCID. Invoke cdecl(callbacks,context,&device,&calibration,parameter0,&addresses,&resultBool): exactly7 pushed arguments and caller ADD ESP,0x1c. EAX is a pointer/reference to vector<string>, copied into controller-owned vector via0x3920; no hidden return-buffer argument is pushed for this plugin ABI. resultBool is a separate output initialized false.","Set context+0x9e8=0. If returned CID vector is empty, invoke cid_alternate with same addresses and bool*. If nonempty original vector, do not use alternate.","callback+0x98(ctx,context[0x9e8]); store uint32 CID count at+0x59c. Copy every CID string including NUL into context+0x118+i*0x22 without a visible count or string truncation guard. Free temporary vectors/strings; FreeLibrary(last global handle), set handle0. Return resultBool.","CPassThruException catch stores exception+0xc into *context+0x754, sets *context+0x974=1 and *context+0x744=1, then follows cleanup/false-result continuation. Not all exception classes are caught here."],"joins":["FlashBackend.CParameter","FlashBackend.CCommunicationAddress","FlashGetters.StartGetCID"],"instruction_pins":["0x1000708b LoadParameter","0x100073ed StartGetCID indirect call","0x10007869 exception mapping","0x100073c9..0x100073f3 seven pushes/call/ADD ESP,0x1c;0x100073fc push EAX to vector copier"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.cid","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.cid_alternate","rva":"0x7c20","abi":{"calling_convention":"MSVC x86 C++ vector<string> hidden sret","inputs":["vector<string>* returnBuffer","address vector*","bool* resultOut"],"result":"vector<string>; same success bool pointer passed to getters"},"ordered_behavior":["Initialize empty result. Read AlternateDLLFileNamesForGetCID with capacity1 into260-byte storage; if first name empty return empty. Read EnableAlternateDLLVersionsInformationForGetCID with capacity1 into adjacent260-byte storage. Loop bound is returned VERSION-entry count, not independently compared to alternate-name count.","For each slot, copy alternate path into context+0x764; extract version to+0x863; resource failure or lexicographically lower version than matching minimum throws9999. Clear both uint32 error slots+0x754/+0x758; load StartGetCID and invoke EXACTLY7 explicit plugin arguments, with vector pointer returned EAX and NO hidden plugin sret. Internal helper7c20 itself uses a separate C++ vector-return buffer; do not conflate the two ABIs. Seven pushes7dfd/7e03/7e09/7e0f/7e14/7e19/7e1f precede indirect call7e25; ADD ESP20 also cleans the prior one-argument loader call.","On first nonempty returned vector set context+0x9e8=1 and return. Otherwise continue. Does not recompute communication addresses for alternate. Does not unload previous primary or previous alternate before overwriting global handle; outer CID cleanup frees only last stored handle. Preserve this handle-lifetime quirk."],"joins":["FlashGetters.StartGetCID"],"instruction_pins":["0x10007cca..0x10007d29 capacity1 accessors","0x10007dcb signed lexical lower gate","0x10007df8 load alternate"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.cid_alternate","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.classic_prepare","rva":"0x8990","abi":{"inputs":["global context and callbacks"],"result":"bool in AL; decompiler primary fragment incorrectly typed void, actual tail0x905f returns saved result"},"ordered_behavior":["For every CPU image i from0 to GetNumCPUImages()-1 load Kind+Contact+CPU(i)+\".ini\" into parameter[i] (stride0x24); SetKeys(kind,CPU(i),contact), with9999 failure. Not only selected CPU is loaded.","Read up to4 GetCANIDFunctionNameForPrepareWrite strings from parameter[currentCPU] into four260-byte slots. If first empty skip resolution. Otherwise construct address resolver(parameter[currentCPU],NULL callbacks,calibration), supply all function strings plus all cached CID strings context+0x118 stride0x22 and count+0x59c. Fail resolution ->9999.","Read DLLFileNameForPrepareWrite, file version and version minimum from parameter[0], even when currentCPU is not0. Load StartPrepareWrite with no retry-pre-IG export requirement. Call(callbacks,context,&device,&calibration,parameter0,&addresses).","If callback+0x48(ctx) !=2 set phase3 regardless of prepare result. Publish *context+0x9e4 via callback+0xa0 and low8(*context+0x9c0) via callback+0xbc. Cleanup temporary vectors, FreeLibrary and zero handle. Return prepare result.","CPassThruException catch maps exception+0xc to error slot+0x754 and sets pointed flags+0x974/+0x744 before cleanup."],"joins":["FlashBackend.CParameter","FlashBackend.CCommunicationAddress","FlashPrepare.StartPrepareWrite"],"instruction_pins":["0x10008f95 call[174d8]","0x10008fab..0x10008fb8 callback+48 phase3 gate","0x1000901b catch","0x1000905f unload/return"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.classic_prepare","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.gateway_mode","rva":"0xa250","abi":{"calling_convention":"cdecl","inputs":["bool priorResult in low8 argument"],"result":"bool in AL; upper24 return bits not defined as semantic output"},"ordered_behavior":["If priorResult false, skip loading and enter failure/retry handling. If true load Kind+Contact+CPU0+\".ini\" into parameter0; SetKeys(kind,CPU0,contact). Get DLLFileNameForChangeToReprogGatewayMode.","If DLL path empty, retain priorResult=true, do not load any gateway module and set phase2. If nonempty, copy name, resolve GetCANIDFunctionNameForChangeToReprogGatewayMode using resolver(parameter0) and no cached CID/location, require file version and minimum, load ChangeToReprogGatewayMode.","Invoke(callbacks,context,&device,&calibration,parameter0,&addresses,&handledBool). handledBool is initialized false. Replace priorResult with callee AL only when handledBool is true; otherwise retain priorResult. Thus false callee return can be ignored by design.","If effective result true set phase2. If false call retry_engine(NULL); if continueFlag *context+0x75c is false set terminal *context+0x744=true. If global module handle nonnull FreeLibrary then zero. Catch PassThru maps exception+0xc, flags+0x974/+0x744 and forces effective result false."],"joins":["FlashBackend.CCommunicationAddress","FlashPrepare.ChangeToReprogGatewayMode"],"instruction_pins":["0x1000a63d..0x1000a651 handledBool override","0x1000a81d catch","0x1000a868 unload"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.gateway_mode","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.classic_write","rva":"0x4c10","abi":{"inputs":["global context and callbacks"],"result":"bool in AL, may be true after a failed writer if retry callbacks clear continueFlag without terminalFlag"},"ordered_behavior":["Preflight ALL CPU images: load Kind+Contact+CPU(i)+\".ini\"/SetKeys into parameter[i]; for nonempty GetCANIDFunctionNameForFlashWrite resolve address list using parameter[i],NULL callbacks,calibration and LocationID(i), no cached CID. Store per-CPU address vectors.","For each preflight CPU get DLLFileNameForFlashWrite, copy name, extract and gate version; read PrepareRetryFlag from parameter[i] but ConfirmAfterEndOfFlashingFlag from parameter[currentCPU]. Load required symbols then immediately unload, leaving function pointer globals intact. All preflight checks occur before first actual write.","Actual end is totalCPU unless CpuLoopBetweenPrepareAndWriteFlag(parameter[currentCPU]) true, in which case end=currentCPU+1. Start actual i=currentCPU. If no loaded module load selected parameter[i] DLL, extract version again (no second minimum comparison), read PrepareRetryFlag(i) and ConfirmAfterEndOfFlashingFlag(currentCPU), resolve exports.","Before each call callback+0x88(ctx) gates cancellation. If true: result=false; refresh phase from callback+0x84, context+0x9e8 from+0x9c, *context+0x9e4 from+0xa4, *context+0xa44 from+0xb8, *context+0x9c0 from low8(callback+0xc0). Then retry_engine(addressVectors).","Otherwise SetCommunicationLogMode(2); StartFlashWrite(callbacks,context,&device,&calibration,parameter[i],&addressVectors); SetCommunicationLogMode(writerResult==false ?1:0). Publish low8(*context+0x760) via callback+0x7c, then phase via callback+0x80. If writer false enter retry_engine.","After retry if continueFlag false and terminalFlag false set return result=true and exit. If continueFlag true, exit when phase==1 OR IGOffRetriableFlag(i) true; otherwise retry same CPU with no fixed retry count or delay in this outer loop.","On write success clear uint32 errors+0x754/+0x758, increment i; if last set notification+0x968=false. Always notification+0x96c=false, *context+0x964=0, continueFlag=0, assign context+0x738=i, unload and zero handle. Before another CPU, callback+0x4c asks FlagToDoIGOFFONAtCPUTypeChange; true exits successful without processing next CPU.","Free address vectors then unload last handle; return result. Catch PassThru stores exception+0xc, sets flags+0x974/+0x744; follow cleanup. There is no blanket rollback of successful prior CPU writes."],"joins":["FlashTransport.CJ2534IF.SetCommunicationLogMode","FlashWriters.StartFlashWrite/PrepareRetry/IsFinishReprogramming"],"instruction_pins":["0x10005219..0x1000524c preflight loader then unload","0x1000540d cancellation","0x10005458 writer call","0x10005768 catch"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.classic_write","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.node_prepare","rva":"0x9370","abi":{"inputs":["global context/callbacks"],"result":"bool in AL"},"ordered_behavior":["Use node=GetNodeIdx(context.currentCPU), required=GetRequiredSpecReproVer(node), CPU string=CPUType(0). If required equals imported RequiredSpecReproVer02 use filename Kind+Contact+CPU0+\".ini\", keys(kind,CPU0,Contact). Else discriminator = ProtocolAtNode(node) for exact Phase6 contact, otherwise required; filename Kind+Contact+discriminator+CPU0+\".ini\", keys(kind,CPU0,Contact+discriminator). Load into parameter0; any false load/keys ->9999.","Get GetCANIDFunctionNameForPrepareWrite from parameter0 into single260-byte string (not list here); nonempty resolves using callbacks/calibration and no cached CID/location. Require file version/minimum and StartPrepareWrite. For exact Phase6 also require ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry.","Call StartPrepareWrite(callbacks,context,&device,&calibration,parameter0,&addresses). Publish low8(*context+0x990) through callback+0x90. Success sets phase2. Failure calls retry_engine(NULL); if continueFlag false set terminalFlag=true, else exact Phase6 calls ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry(callbacks,context,&device,&calibration).","Cleanup vectors, unload and zero handle. PassThru catch maps exception+0xc and pointed flags+0x974/+0x744."],"joins":["FlashShared.CalibrationFile node properties","FlashPrepare.StartPrepareWrite/ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry"],"instruction_pins":["0x1000943a required-version branch","0x10009b4e prepare call","0x10009bd5 phase2 success","0x10009d0a catch"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.node_prepare","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.node_write","rva":"0x5c30","abi":{"inputs":["global context/callbacks"],"result":"bool in AL; cancellation recovery can return true without writer success"},"ordered_behavior":["Capture currentCPU and node index. Default parameter-load start=currentCPU. If signed node field at calibration node table+node*0xc0+0x7c is >0, set start=sum CPU-count dwords at node-table+i*0xc0 for i<node. End=count of all CPU images whose GetNodeIdx(i)<=node. The raw node+0x7c field is not named here; preserve its signed-positive gate.","Load parameter[start..end) using same required-version/discriminator rule as node_prepare; all use CPUType(0), node/required/protocol queried from context.currentCPU. Node count table uses global17540 imported CalibrationFile internal pointer. This is not simply totalCPU or all subsequent nodes.","Get selected currentCPU GetCANIDFunctionNameForFlashWrite single string; allocate outer vector with one address vector. Resolve with callbacks/calibration and no cached CIDs/location. Read selected DLL and require version+minimum. Load StartFlashWrite; PrepareRetry and IsFinishReprogramming are looked up but not required (false flags). Exact Phase6 requires ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry.","For each i from captured currentCPU to end: cancellation callback+0x88(ctx) true sets result=false and stores callback+0x94(ctx) byte through context+0x990, then recovery. Otherwise logMode2, writer(callbacks,context,&device,&calibration,parameter[i],&oneAddressVector), logMode(result==false?1:0).","Failure or cancellation: retry_engine(NULL). If continueFlag false and terminalFlag false return true. If continueFlag true AND exact Phase6 call ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry. Break regardless; this function does not loop back to same writer after recovery.","Success clears errors, increments i; final i==end clears notification+0x968. Always clears notification+0x96c, *context+0x964,continueFlag. If signed raw node+0x7c>0 BREAK BEFORE writing context.currentCPU=i; otherwise assign currentCPU=i and continue. Hence grouped node case preserves original CPU index here.","Cleanup vectors then unload and zero handle. PassThru catch maps error and pointed flags+0x974/+0x744. No automatic phase reset after success."],"joins":["FlashShared.CalibrationFile.GetNodeIdx/GetRequiredSpecReproVer/GetProtocolAtNode","FlashWriters.StartFlashWrite/ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry"],"instruction_pins":["0x10005cbf..0x10005e66 node index/count derivation","0x1000666c loader flags0,0,Phase6","0x100066c7 cancellation","0x100067ca node+7c early break","0x100069a5 catch"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.node_write","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.retry_engine","rva":"0x3b90","abi":{"calling_convention":"cdecl","inputs":["optional vector<vector<CommunicationAddress>>* addresses; accepted but not used as outbound frame buffer in this body"],"result":"void, mutates pointed context state"},"ordered_behavior":["Save original uint32 errors *context+0x754 and +0x758. Read IGOffRetriableFlag defaultfalse from parameter0 for exact P5_Unified contact, else parameter[currentCPU]. If false AND phase2 AND errorKind==2, change errorKind to4.","Call reconnect_engine(continueFlag,error1,error2,errorKind,terminalFlag); then callback+0x20(ctx). While continueFlag true and phase2, execute following policy. No fixed retry counter exists.","If IGOffRetriableFlag false, callback+0x4c(ctx,kind,CPU(currentCPU),contact,\"FlagToCancelAutomaticIGOFF\",bool* defaultfalse). If it returns true and callback+0x74(ctx) returns false, set errorKind3 and reprompt via reconnect_engine then callback+0x20.","Otherwise if !IGOffRetriable AND context byte+0x980 true: if *context+0x990==1 call callback+0x78(ctx,true) and remember this action; callback+0x38(ctx) false sets errorKind5 if action was sent, else3, then reprompt. If gate passes continue.","Set *context+0x964=true. Read PrepareRetryFlag(parameter[currentCPU]) defaultfalse; if false break. When !IGOffRetriable AND (*context+0x9c0==2 OR byte(*(context+8)+0x78)!=0), call callback+0x78(ctx,true) and remember action.","Restore saved error1/error2; read signed ReceiveTimeoutBeforePrepareRetry default0. If >0 call device.SetTimeout(uint32 timeout), with no restore in this controller. Invoke PrepareRetry(callbacks,context,&device,&calibration,parameter[currentCPU]). If true clear error1/error2 then break.","PrepareRetry false: read FlagToNonSetEerrorKindConnect (exact shipped spelling), defaultfalse. If false set errorKind to5 when action remembered else3. callback+0x14(ctx), reconnect_engine, callback+0x20(ctx), loop while continueFlag true.","After loop, if continueFlag && phase2: read ConfirmAfterEndOfFlashingFlag defaultfalse. If true read IGOffRetriableFlag again. If !IGOffRetriable OR context byte+0x970 true: Sleep(5000), then only if +0x970 true perform finish confirmation. Thus the delay may occur without confirmation when !IGOffRetriable and +0x970 false.","Confirmation resolves up to4 GetCANIDFunctionNameForPrepareWrite functions with cached CIDs using parameter[currentCPU] resolver, no callbacks. This resolution is performed even though IsFinishReprogramming receives ONLY(callbacks,&device). Address resolution failure throws9999. True finish result clears continueFlag, callback+0x1c(ctx), notification+0x968=false, notification+0x96c=false. Free confirmation vectors.","Finally if no earlier callback+0x78 action AND continueFlag && !IGOffRetriable && phase2, call callback+0x78(ctx,true). Do not infer a successful flash solely from retry-engine return; callers interpret continueFlag/terminalFlag separately."],"joins":["FlashTransport.CJ2534IF.SetTimeout","FlashWriters.PrepareRetry","FlashWriters.IsFinishReprogramming","FlashBackend.CCommunicationAddress"],"instruction_pins":["0x10003c50 IGOffRetriable","0x10003d39 callback+4c six arguments","0x10003ed5..0x10003f04 PrepareRetry","0x1000407c Sleep5000","0x1000440e..0x10004423 finish call","0x100044ca callback+78(ctx,1)"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.retry_engine","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.reconnect_engine","rva":"0x4780","abi":{"calling_convention":"cdecl","inputs":["bool* continueFlag","uint32* error1","uint32* error2","uint32* errorKind","bool* terminalFlag"],"result":"void"},"ordered_behavior":["First invoke callbacks+0x14(ctx),+0x18(ctx),+0x60(ctx,device.GetOpenedDevice()). Clear *continueFlag=false; invoke callbacks+0x1c(ctx),+0x0c(ctx),+0x20(ctx). Set device.OpenedDevice from callback+0x64(ctx) bool. If continueFlag remains false set terminalFlag=true and return. Callback writes to shared context supply the new flag; this controller does not set it true.","If continueFlag true clear both errors and call device.Disconnect; catch-all suppresses Disconnect exceptions and continues to connect attempt.","Select numeric J2534 protocol: default6; exact SIL->3; exact Ethernet->0x8013; exact P5_Unified or Phase6 uses0x8012 only if ProtocolAtNode(GetNodeIdx(currentCPU)) exactly equals imported DIAG_COMM_PROTOCOL_CANFD, else6. Other contacts retain6. Call device.Connect(protocol).","Read voltage via ControlIO(IOCTL3,NULL,&uint32mV). Convert unsigned uint32 to double and divide1000; implementation uses signed CVTDQ2PD +4294967296 correction for high bit, so no signed-negative voltage interpretation. Read helper initializes double0 and catches all IOCTL exceptions, returning0. Require strict voltage>1.0; <=1.0 throws CPassThruException1008(0x3f0).","FH3 FuncInfo16170 proves FIRST typed catch is CJ2534Exception (TypeDescriptor17288, handler4a16): copies exception+0xc/+0x2c to error1/error2, sets errorKind3, callback+0x14(ctx), failed attempt. SECOND typed catch is CPassThruException (TypeDescriptor17240, handler4a8a): copies exception+0xc only, sets errorKind3 and failed attempt, leaves error2 unchanged. Raw TryBlockMap/HandlerType and handler instructions pinned in source-bound raw/typed evidence names are not inferred from field offsets.","After each attempt export device to context+0x54, callback+0x8c(ctx). If failed attempt, repeat initial callbacks/state negotiation; if continueFlag true clear errors, suppress Disconnect exceptions and try Connect again. If false set terminalFlag=true. Successful connect/voltage exits without another negotiation. No attempt limit exists in this body."],"joins":["FlashTransport.CJ2534IF.Connect/Disconnect/ControlIO/ExportData","FH3 typed CJ2534Exception incoming from FlashTransport.J2534IF and CPassThruException (constructor imported tcuwexception.dll/FlashShared); exact class names, not offset-based type or module-ownership inference"],"instruction_pins":["0x100047d2..0x1000484e callback order","0x1000487a disconnect catchall","0x100049ed Connect","0x10004a16 primary catch","0x10004a54 ExportData then callback+8c","0x1000a1de ControlIO3","0x1000a1ef unsigned correction","0x1000a21d exception continuation returns double0"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.reconnect_engine","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.version_gate","rva":"0x3a30","abi":{"calling_convention":"cdecl","inputs":["const char* actualVersion","CParameter* parameter"],"result":"bool in AL"},"ordered_behavior":["Initialize false; GetParameters(\"EnableDLLVersionInformation\",four260-byte slots,&count initialized4). Only if returned count==4 compare actualVersion with slot[context.phase].","Unsigned-byte lexicographic NUL-terminated strcmp semantics: accept actual>=minimum, including equality. This is NOT numeric dotted-version ordering (\"10\" sorts before\"2\"). There is no phase<4 guard; current legitimate phases0..3 select CID/prepare/write/gateway slots respectively.","Accessor return ignored. Catch-all returns initial false. No alternate delimiter, normalization, trimming or semantic-version parsing is performed."],"joins":["FlashBackend.CParameter.GetParameters"],"instruction_pins":["0x10003aee..0x10003b13 lexical compare","0x10003b15 catchall","0x10003b21 AL return"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.version_gate","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.file_version","rva":"0x7f90","abi":{"calling_convention":"cdecl","inputs":["LPCSTR filename","char* outputVersion"],"result":"bool in AL"},"ordered_behavior":["GetFileVersionInfoSizeA(filename,&handle). Zero ->false. Allocate returned byte count and call GetFileVersionInfoA(filename,0,size,buffer). Failure ->false. Get translation table via VerQueryValueA(buffer,\"\\VarFileInfo\\Translation\",&ptr,&bytes); failure->false.","For each of bytes>>2 translation pairs (uint16 language,uint16 codepage) in original order build exact \"StringFileInfo\\%04x%04x\\\" then append\"FileVersion\". Query this path; first successful query wins, copy NUL-terminated string verbatim to outputVersion without output-length bound and returntrue. Ignore fixed-file-version numeric fields.","After translation query (including translation-query false), iteration exhaustion, query success or caught exception, free resource buffer through common continuation. Catch-all returns false. GetFileVersionInfoA failure after successful allocation follows directfalse return before common free; preserve that allocation-lifetime quirk."],"joins":["Windows.VERSION resource-only offline semantics"],"instruction_pins":["0x10007fef..0x10008034 version APIs","0x10008465..0x1000849a cleanup/false","data0x1001369c \"FileVersion\""],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.file_version","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.loaders","rva":"0x8640/0x86e0/0x8780/0x88c0","abi":{"calling_convention":"cdecl","inputs":["LPCSTR path","per-loader bool requirement flags"],"result":"void; throws9999 on missing required import"},"ordered_behavior":["Each LoadLibraryA writes global handle174d0. CID requires StartGetCID->174d4. Gateway requires ChangeToReprogGatewayMode->174dc. Prepare requires StartPrepareWrite->174d8; if its flag true also ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry->174ec.","Flash resolves StartFlashWrite->174e0 (always required), PrepareRetry->174e4 (required iff flag1), IsFinishReprogramming->174e8 (required iff flag2); iff flag3 resolve ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry->174ec and require it. Missing optional exports are null, not synthesized implementations.","All LoadLibrary/export failures construct CPassThruException9999 with source-line/message pins. Loader itself does not FreeLibrary on a missing export. Calling phase cleanup owns last global handle. Pointers are not all reset on unload and pre-IG pointer is not refreshed when flag3 false; subsequent paths must preserve existing loader policy."],"joins":["FlashGetters.StartGetCID","FlashPrepare.StartPrepareWrite/ChangeToReprogGatewayMode","FlashWriters.StartFlashWrite/PrepareRetry/IsFinishReprogramming/ProcessBeforeIGOffOnAtRetry"],"instruction_pins":["0x100087a1 LoadLibrary null","0x100087bd required StartFlashWrite","0x100087e4 optional flag1","0x1000880b optional flag2","0x1000881c flag3","0x1000885d exception9999"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.loaders","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.phases.dll_lifetime","rva":"0xb980","abi":{"calling_convention":"stdcall DllMain-style three args, RET0xc","inputs":["module","DWORD reason","reserved"],"result":"BOOL true on ordinary completion"},"ordered_behavior":["On reason1 allocate glngNUM_CPU_MAXNUM CParameter objects of stride0x24 with a4-byte array-count cookie, run constructors, publish global parameter pointer174f8. Multiplication/addition overflow saturation follows generated vector-new pattern.","On reason0, if parameter pointer nonnull, run per-element destructors via cookie, sized delete array, set pointer0. Other reasons returntrue without per-thread work.","No per-Execute allocation of parameter array, no clearing array between successive phase calls, no per-session indexing apart from CPU slot. CJ2534IF100175b8 and CalibrationFile10017500 are module-global objects."],"joins":["FlashBackend.CParameter.constructor/destructor","FlashShared.CommonDefinitions.glngNUM_CPU_MAXNUM"],"instruction_pins":["0x1000b9b6 imported count","0x1000ba03 vector ctor stride0x24","0x1000ba08 global pointer store","0x1000ba39 vector destructor","0x1000ba74 ret0xc"],"contract_id":"flashbackend.phases.dll_lifetime","component":"phases","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.backend","cuw_utility.core","cuw_utility.entry"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.bytes.storage","module":"TCUWBytes.dll","inputs":{"this":"CBytes size0x408; bytes[512]@0, signed long count@0x200, limit512@0x204, scratch512@0x208"},"semantics":["Empty constructor zeros bytes and count; limit=512. uint16/uint32 constructors emit2/4 big-endian bytes; raw constructor memcpys caller signed count and writes count, no bound validation.","Assignment self-check, zeros512 then memcpy source.count and copies count; destructor no-op. Equality compares count then exact bytes, inequality negates it. Both index operators unchecked (mutable returns this+index; const returns byte). Clear zeros512/count, retains limit."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.bytes.storage","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWBytes.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.bytes.numeric","module":"TCUWBytes.dll","inputs":{"count":"signed long32","SetNum.new":"signed long32"},"semantics":["GetUnsignedLong: result=OR_{i=0..count-1}(byte[count-1-i] << ((8*i)&31)); count<=0 gives0. Normal up-to4-byte interpretation big endian, larger count retains actual x86 masked shift behavior.","GetUnsignedShort analog uses16bit accumulator and x86 shift counts, low16 result.","SetNum identical count no-op; otherwise copies old-count bytes to scratch, zeros512 bytes; if growing copies old bytes to this+(new-old) (left zero pad); if shrinking copies new bytes from scratch+(old-new) (keep least-significant trailing bytes); writes new count. No sign/capacity check."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.bytes.numeric","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWBytes.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.bytes.hex","module":"TCUWBytes.dll","inputs":{"hex":"NUL terminated ASCII","output":"char* plus signed long capacity"},"semantics":["Hex constructor zero initializes, rejects odd strlen with CException; sets count=strlen/2 then strtol(two-char NUL temporary,base16), requires end byte NUL; stores low8 result. Invalid hex throws CException; no512 bound. strtol accepts leading whitespace or sign if complete two-character pair conversion consumes through NUL.","SetBytesFromHexString rejects odd strlen with CException, sets count before parsing then uses helper10001060 on each two-character std::string: length<=2; character dispatch accepts ONLY ASCII0..9,A..F,a..f, otherwise CException. Accumulator=(acc<<4)+nibble, returns low8. No strtol, no whitespace/sign acceptance, no512 bound. Prefix mutation/count persist if later pair throws.","ConvBytesToString emits uppercase high/low hex and NUL only if outputCapacity-1 >= 2*count (signed comparison); insufficient output leaves destination unchanged. GetString delegates using own byte count."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.bytes.hex","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWBytes.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.bytes.checksum-endian","module":"TCUWBytes.dll","inputs":{"width":"uint32 bytes per group;0 means full count"},"semantics":["CalcCheckSum returns sum(bytes[0:count]) modulo256, empty/nonpositive count returns0.","ConvEndian computes width=arg or count if0, unsigned count/width, reverses each complete width-byte chunk in place, leaves incomplete tail. Empty count+width0 executes division by zero; no guard."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.bytes.checksum-endian","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWBytes.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.parameter.load","module":"TCUWParameterForVC.dll","inputs":{"filename":"ANSI char*","keyColumn":"ANSI char* or null"},"semantics":["Path=drive+directory of GetModuleFileNameA(NULL)+\"ini\\\"+filename. _sopen_dispatch flags0x8000/share0x40; open/seek=-1/read=-1 returnfalse with close/free ordering. Read count other than-1 is not compared to expected file length.","Free old encoded-storage, Delete old table. Allocate floor(fileLength/2)+2 zero bytes. For every input pair (a,b), output=((a>>2)*16+(b>>2)+120)&255; loop increments2 until >=fileLength, so odd length reads beyond pair. Set decoded[floor(length/2)]=0xFF terminator; parse via ReadData.","Lookup supplied keyColumn else exact \"ParamFileKeySystemProtocolMicon\"; store column@this+0x20; return parserResult && keyColumnIndex!=-1."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.parameter.load","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWParameterForVC.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.parameter.csv","module":"TCUWParameterForVC.dll","inputs":{"input":"decoded byte sequence terminated0xFF"},"semantics":["Deletes prior table then stores vector<row> (12-byte vector), each row vector<cell>12, each cell vector<MSVC2015string>24. First row becomes headers.","Fields comma separated; initial quote selects quote terminator, doubled quotes append one quote. LF within scan splits cell into multiple string values. CRLF outside quoted field terminates a row; CRLF inside quoted field remains field content by source branch.","1024-byte stack accumulator repeatedly strncat(...,1) without remaining capacity; no bounded-field rejection. At row boundary column-count mismatch returnsfalse, leaving earlier parsed table data. Terminal0xFF returns true after cleanup of temporary vectors; not general RFC4180 parser."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.parameter.csv","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWParameterForVC.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.parameter.keys","module":"TCUWParameterForVC.dll","inputs":{"keys":["arg1 kind","arg2 CPU","arg3 contact/context"]},"semantics":["Column search compares first string of each header cell sequentially; first exact byte/length match wins. Row search records1..N uses selected key column first string, first exact match wins, returns-1 otherwise.","SetKeys concatenates arg1+arg3+arg2 without delimiter; stores resulting row index@+0x1c even if-1. WithKeys uses same concatenation but local row, does not change selected row.","Out-of-range row/column GetData returns shared empty vector@this+0xc. IsExistParameter checks column existence only, not current selected-row cell."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.parameter.keys","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWParameterForVC.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.parameter.scalar","module":"TCUWParameterForVC.dll","inputs":{"result":"bool success plus caller-owned char*/long32*/bool8*"},"semantics":["Missing column/row/empty cell-value vector returnsfalse without output mutation. String scalar copies first string through NUL with no output capacity.","Long strtol(firstValue,base10); rejects only result0 && end!=NUL && end==start; empty string parses0 successfully; numeric prefixes/trailing suffix accepted; no errno/overflow check.","Bool calls long then writes long!=0 only on success (negative true), not recovery INI >0 convention."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.parameter.scalar","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWParameterForVC.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.parameter.vector","module":"TCUWParameterForVC.dll","inputs":{"output":"flat contiguous char slots stride260, despite exported PAPAD spelling","inoutCount":"signed long capacity->actual count"},"semantics":["Find selected/exact keyed cell; missing or zero values ->false unchanged outputs.","Copies up to input capacity strings (each unbounded NUL copy into260-byte slot), then writes actual source count even if truncated. Returns true. Consumers iterating returned count without capacity check preserve overread risk; no pretend min-count output."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.parameter.vector","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWParameterForVC.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.address.select","module":"TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll","inputs":{"this":"CCommunicationAddress parameter*@0, vector<packed7>@4, callbacks*@0x10,calibration*@0x14","args":["ordered vector<string> strategy names","bool* success","optional vector<string>* CIDs","optional string* LocationID"]},"semantics":["Clear output vector and success=false. For each strategy exact case-sensitive name dispatch; assign strategy bool to success; stop after first false, continue after true. Not try-until-success fallback. Unknown strategy leaves previous bool unchanged; therefore unknown first stops false, unknown after successful step retains true. Return const reference own vector+4.","Strategies: GetCanIDsFromParamForGetCID,ForPrepareWrite,MatchedPartOfCIDForPrepareWrite,RespondCID,ForReprogGateway,FromLocationIDForWrite,FromResultOfGetCID,FromCANIDTable,FromCalibrationFileForSUZUKI. Preserve caller-provided order. Empty list returns empty,false."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.address.select","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.address.split","module":"TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll","inputs":{"output":"packed7 bytes:request[3],response[3],flag8"},"semantics":["Unbounded NUL copy to20byte stack local. strtok(\"/\") yields request then response; null token unchecked. Clears output7. Request strlen==6 selects width3,flag1 else width2,flag0. Decode both using CBytes hex constructor then SetNum(width); copy width bytes toreq0..2 andresp3..5. Invalid hex throws; non6 lengths still coerced width2, do not invent length validation."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.address.split","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.address.parameter","module":"TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll","inputs":{"keys":["CanIDForGetCID","CanIDForPrepareWrite","CanIDForReprogGateway","CIDForCalcCpuNum","CanIDMatchedPartOfCID"]},"semantics":["Generic GetCanIDsFromParam gets multi-values capacity10 into contiguous260byte slots; actual returned count drives loop, each value passed split and appended to caller output; no output clear here. Failed parameter query returnsfalse.","MatchedPartOfCID variant queries CIDForCalcCpuNum; first value exact \"*\" counts all supplied CIDs, otherwise counts supplied CIDs whose text begins at position0 with ANY configured prefix; each CID counted once; empty prefix matches. If count>=2 append CanIDMatchedPartOfCID addresses; otherwise return original successful query bool without append.","RespondCID variant appends CanIDForPrepareWrite list, then repeats ORIGINAL output address count once for every additional CID (CID count>1), preserving duplicate address records."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.address.parameter","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.address.table","module":"TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll","inputs":{"calibration":"GetNumNode/GetDiagID","callback":"callbacks+0x5c(ctx,DiagID,\"ResponseCANID\",buffer)"},"semantics":["Iterate all calibration nodes; callback returns response textual ID; empty result stops traversal. Decode request DiagID and response CBytes directly (no SetNum). Pack first2 or3 bytes based only request text strlen==6; append each successful record. Returntrue iff number appended>=1 AND equals node count. Partial appended prefix retained onfalse."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.address.table","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.address.suzuki","module":"TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll","inputs":{"calibration":"model string@0x4c(request) and0x7c(response), lengths@0x5c/0x8c"},"semantics":["If either string length0 returnfalse. Decode both hex CBytes; append request first2 bytes,response first2 bytes,flag0. Third request/response bytes local not explicitly assigned by this body (consumers use width2). Returntrue. No remote discovery performed by helper."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.address.suzuki","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll"]},
  {"id":"flashbackend.address.location","module":"TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll","inputs":{"LocationID":"hex string"},"semantics":["Decode LocationID; append packed record with request=location bytes2,3; response=bytes0,1; third byte for each0; flag0.","Append second record request0720/flag0 when location bytes6,7 equal07,20; otherwise request0740FE/flag1. Response bytes in second local record are not assigned in this body (stack indeterminate bytes preserved); do not invent response ID. Always returnstrue if decoding did not throw."],"component":"helpers","contract_id":"flashbackend.address.location","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCommunicationAddress.dll"]},
