  {"id":"backend.calibration.zip-extract","source":"CUWAccessZIP.dll","methoddef":"0x06000001","input":{"source":"System.String path","destination":"System.String path (directory of this path is extraction root)"},"result":{"type":"enum int32","0":"success after all entries","1":"initial result retained for caught ZIP failure before success assignment"},"ordered_behavior":["Set result=1. Build temp=Combine(GetDirectoryName(destination),GetFileName(source)).","If temp.ToLower ends .cuwc or .scuw, replace final four characters with zip; overwrite-copy source to temp; read all bytes. Otherwise overwrite-copy source to temp unchanged.","Wrapped branch scans for bytewise case-insensitive ASCII [DataCompression] using Shift-JIS bytes; each character may match lowercase OR uppercase. First full match sets offset=markerEnd+1, not CRLF-aware. No match leaves offset=0 unless a partial suffix throws indexing exception.","Write bytes[offset:] back to temp; ZipFile.OpenRead(temp); enumerate EVERY ZipArchive.Entries entry in library order.","For each entry p=Path.Combine(GetDirectoryName(destination),entry.FullName). If directory entry Name==empty create p if absent; otherwise ensure parent(p) exists. Nonempty Name uses ExtractToFile(entry,p,true).","Enumerator and archive disposed via finally. After enumeration+enumerator disposal, assign result=0 BEFORE archive disposal. Catch around ZipFile.OpenRead through archive disposal swallows exception and returns current result, not unconditional1."],"selection":"No CUW-only filter, first-member selection, target-CID selection, or archive member deduplication. FullName is passed directly to Path.Combine; no explicit containment/traversal predicate in this method.","cleanup":"No delete of temp zip, already-extracted files, or created directories, including error cases. Sequential repeated file paths overwrite.","quirks":["Copied .scuw/.cuwc loses exactly4 suffix chars and appends zip; marker skip is exactly one byte after closing bracket.","Unbounded marker scan can index past byte array near EOF; this preparation exception escapes, NOT result1.","No explicit ZIP size/count/decompression limit.","Archive disposal failure after success assignment is swallowed with result0."],"errors":"Path/suffix/copy/read/marker scan/array copy/write preparation precedes catch and exceptions PROPAGATE. Only ZipFile.OpenRead, entry enumeration/extraction and finally disposal are caught. Usually caught failure returns initial1; archive.Dispose throwing after result=0 still returns0.","contract_id":"backend.calibration.zip-extract","component":"calibration","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.CUWAccessZIP.dll"]},
  {"id":"backend.calibration.zip-header","source":"CUWAccessZIP.dll","methoddef":"0x06000002","input":{"path":"string","header":"out string"},"result":{"0":"marker found at nonzero byte offset","2":"no nonzero marker offset"},"behavior":["Initialize result2 and out header=empty. ReadAllBytes(path); scan same Shift-JIS lowercase-or-uppercase [DataCompression] bytes.","On first full match, record START of marker. If start !=0, copy prefix[0:start], decode shift_jis to out header and return0. Otherwise return2."],"errors":"No local catch; file/encoding/index/overflow exceptions propagate. Marker at file offset0 is indistinguishable from no match. Scan does not cap i+j to file length.","contract_id":"backend.calibration.zip-header","component":"calibration","owner":"FlashBackend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.CUWAccessZIP.dll"]},
