  {"id":"FlashTransport.Socket.RawReceive","entries":["0x10003610","0x10003770","0x100033a0","0x10003f20"],"typed_inputs":["buffer:char*","length_inout:i32* (input maximum; output successful actual recv length)","UDP additionally source_out:sockaddr_in*","timeout_ms:u32 Get/Set"],"ordered_behavior":["Require valid stored socket. fd_set count1 + socket; timeout=(ms/1000,(ms%1000)*1000), initialized once per call. select(0,&readfds,NULL,NULL,&timeval). On nonzero (including-1), call __WSAFDIsSet; if false repeat select after restoring fd_set (same timeval).","When set, TCP recv(socket,buffer,*length,0) or UDP recvfrom(...,source,&len16). Return successful positive byte count through *length; no accumulation. select0 throws timeout CWinSockException2. recv0 or-1 throws CWinSockException1."],"errors_cleanup":["No cancel predicate, total monotonic deadline, receive capacity validation or reconnect. select error is not directly handled as error; may loop via FD predicate. Timeout originates native error2 not ECU response-pending."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWWinSockIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.Socket.PayloadReceive","entries":["0x100038f0"],"typed_inputs":["buffer:char*","length_out:i32* (initial value ignored)","record_last:bool"],"ordered_behavior":["Require TCP valid. RawRecvTCP(buffer,&n=8) exactly ONCE. Decode declared payload lengthBE32 from buffer[4:8] regardless actual returned header length. RawRecvTCP(same buffer,&declared_length) exactly ONCE; overwrite header. *length_out=actual second recv count, not declared header count. If record_last call LastMessage(payload,actual,false)."],"errors_cleanup":["No validation of header protocol/inverse/type, buffer capacity, short first header or partial payload; no reassembly/recv-exact. Zero declared length leads recv0->error1. This faithfully preserves native defect."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWWinSockIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.Socket.Send","entries":["0x100039a0","0x10003a30","0x10003ae0"],"typed_inputs":["msg:const char*","length:i32","TCP record_last:bool"],"ordered_behavior":["TCP: if record_last snapshot msg+8,length-8 before socket validation. Require TCP valid; send(TCP,msg,length,0) once; only -1 fails. Short/zero send treated success, no retransmit.","UDP: require valid UDP; construct sockaddr family2, address htonl(0xffffffff), porthtons13400, restzero; sendto once with flags0,len16; only -1 fails. This is broadcast discovery transport; no message construction here.","SendMsgWithReceiveACKForTCP: if requested snapshot once itself then call SendMsgForTCP(...,same bool), duplicating snapshot; use stack0x1020-byte buffer, RecvPayloadMsgForTCP repeatedly until response[0:2]==request[10:12] and response[2:4]==request[8:10]. Does NOT inspect ACK type/status or require payload>=4."],"errors_cleanup":["ACK loop ignores unmatched frames indefinitely except each raw receive timeout. It consumes unrelated responses; no cancel/reconnect/negative ACK interpretation in this layer."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWWinSockIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.Socket.LastMessage","entries":["0x10003e10","0x10003f10"],"typed_inputs":["payload:const char*","payload_length:u32","is_tx:bool","sink:_typMessageCommunicatedWithECU* supplied by caller"],"ordered_behavior":["No-op unless sink!=NULL and length>=5. sink.type@0=2; sink.length@4=payload_length-2. Copy payload[4:] of length-4 into sink+10 (capacity0x1020); sink+8,+9=TX payload[2:4] or RX payload[0:2]. Thus snapshot keeps peer address plus diagnostic payload, strips opposite address.","Oversize copy (>0x1020) zeros0x1020 and invokes CRT invalid-parameter path, errnoERANGE34; null source/destination errnoEINVAL22. No ECU parse. Pointer setter merely borrows sink."],"errors_cleanup":[],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWWinSockIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.Socket.SyncPeriodic","entries":["0x100033b0","0x10003be0","0x10003d3e","0x10003d50","0x10003f00","0x10003f30","0x10004040","0x100040a0","0x100040c0"],"typed_inputs":["Start(msg:const char*,length:u32,interval_ms:u32,poll_sleep_ms:u32,post_send_hold_ms:u32,receive_ack:bool)","Lock/Unlock/Stop/SetLocalTimeToPrevSendTime noargs"],"ordered_behavior":["Start frees previous message, alloc/copies length, stores interval@14/poll@18/hold@38/ack@24, stopbyte@10=0. Creates suspended worker@0xc, named mutex EXCLUSIVE_OF_WINSOCK_API_ON_CUW_PLUS@3c, then resumes. No allocation/thread/mutex result checks, no previous-worker join. Previous timeSYSTEMTIME@26 only set by explicit setter or send loop.","Worker while !stop: local-clock millisecond difference from previous time, adding24hours iff current.hour<previous.hour. If less interval sleep poll. When due wait mutex100ms repeatedly only while thread handle!=0, send saved msg either raw or ACK path with snapshot=false. Catch-all at3d3e resumes common post-send path (swallows exceptions).","If hold>0, update previous time BEFORE Sleep(hold) while mutex held; then release mutex if threadfield!=0. If hold==0, update previous AFTER release. Repeat. Lock waits100ms until WAIT_OBJECT_0 while threadfield!=0; WAIT_ABANDONED is not treated success. Unlock releases only while threadfield!=0.","Stop sets stopbyte1; while handle!=0 Sleep(poll), WaitForSingleObject(thread,0), clear handle iff result0 or0x80; then CloseHandle(mutex),zero mutex. Does not CloseHandle(thread)."],"errors_cleanup":["No cooperative cancel within blocking send/ACK/read; stop waits until worker returns. Wait failures can cause infinite loop; no bounded join. Catch-all swallowing applies only send body, post-send common path still executes."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWWinSockIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.DeviceValue","entries":["0x10001060","0x100010a0","0x10001210","0x10001250","0x100012d0","0x10001300","0x10001310","0x10001320","0x10001350"],"typed_inputs":["CJ2534Device* this (0x30bytes)","device_name/dll_name:const char* null-terminated; assignment const CJ2534Device&"],"ordered_behavior":["Two MSVC std::string24 fields at+0 device name and+18 DLL name. Default AND private copy constructor create empty strings (copy does not copy). operator= copies both names, setters strlen+assign, getters borrow inline(<=15chars)/heap pointer, Clear sets lengths0 preserving allocated capacity; destructor destroys both. No registry discovery in this class."],"errors_cleanup":[],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.Lifetime","entries":["0x10001720","0x10001730","0x10001970","0x10001a00","0x10001a10","0x10001ac0","0x10001cc0","0x10003760","0x10005190"],"typed_inputs":["CJ2534IF* this (0x1e0bytes)","Open(spec_enum:i32), where2 means J2534-2, other means default"],"ordered_behavior":["Ctor installs vftable: destructor@+0,DoCoreProcessOfConnection@+4,Disconnect@+8,ControlIO@+c,StartSilMsgFilter@+10,SetConfigurationParametersForCanFD@+14. Defaults opened=false,deviceID0,protocol0,channel0,shimModule0,driverLoaded=false,recvTimeout0,sendTimeout1000,SILbaud10400,CANbaud500000,filtercount2,filterIDs0/activefalse,voltage_on=false,paddingtrue,lastsnapshotenabledtrue,periodicfields0,ownershipfields0,all16 driverfunction slotszero. CString descriptor device pointerNULL. Private copy sets only vtable; assignment no-op.","Open calls shim.PassThruOpen(spec==2?\"J2534-2:\":NULL,&deviceID); nonzero throws CJ2534Exception(status), sets openedtrue only success. Close iff opened calls PassThruClose(deviceID), IGNORES returned error, zeros deviceID/opened. UnloadDLL iff shimModule!=0 invokes PassThruUnloadLibrary ignoring status, marks driverLoadedfalse but retains shim module and bound functions.","Clear calls virtual Disconnect first, FreeLibrary(shimModule)/FreeLibrary(MsgDatCommWrapper), destroys selected device, frees04periodicbuffer, closes ownershipacquired/release eventhandles. It resets deviceID/opened/protocol/channel/connected/timeouts/baud/voltage/padding/filtercount2 and IDs/activeflags/functionslots19c..1dc, driverLoadedfalse, vendor symbol string; memset38..73 zeroes periodic state including05bufferpointerWITHOUT freeing old05buffer. It DOES NOT reset snapshotpointer90, snapshotenable94, or ownershipthread80 after Disconnect. Destructor frees selected-device and04/05periodicbuffers but DOES NOT Disconnect/Close/Unload/stopthread."],"errors_cleanup":["Partial connection errors are not rolled back inside Connect; caller is responsible for Disconnect/Clear. Native destructor is not RAII transport teardown.","Private copy/default alias behavior preserved; invalid state imported into object is not sanitized."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.Connect","entries":["0x10001cf0","0x10001d5f","0x10001f80","0x10004fe0","0x10005048","0x1000511e"],"typed_inputs":["protocolID:u32","selected device DLL/name already imported through typJ2534IF"],"ordered_behavior":["Connect delegates virtual DoCoreProcessOfConnection(protocol). Core: HaveOwnership; enable snapshot, zero0x1028 snapshot if supplied; LoadDLL(selected DLL); classify device wireless kind. If DSTi set vendor interface(0,0) then(1,0). PassThruOpen(protocol==0x8012?\"J2534-2:\":NULL,&deviceID), opened=true. If MongoosePro and wireless predicate true: Close then throw CJ2534Exception0 (wireless programming rejection). Any exception from the Mongoose wireless probe is swallowed by catch100020a3 and connection proceeds; only explicit true result rejects.","PassThruConnect(deviceID,protocolID,flags,baud,&channelID): protocol3=>flags0x1200/baud10400;5=>flags0/baud500000;6 or8012=>flags0x900/baud500000;8013=>flags0x10000/baud0; allother flags0/baud0. Nonzero status throws. Success sets protocol and connected=true. protocol3 installs SIL filters. For8012, Connect wrapper invokes FDconfig(true); on ANY exception from that invocation, virtual Disconnect, redo virtual DoCoreProcessOfConnection(original protocol), then FDconfig(false). Only this config-specific fallback is automatic; second failure propagates.","SwitchConnection disconnects existing channel (stops SIL filters if oldprotocol3) ignoring driverDisconnect result, zeroes protocol/connected; normally no close/open/unload/reacquire or periodic-stop. Reconnect same PassThruConnect matrix then filters3. For8012, FDconfig(true); any exception invokes full virtual Disconnect then virtual DoCoreProcessOfConnection(protocol), then FDconfig(false). This exceptional fallback DOES perform complete close/reopen/ownership lifecycle."],"errors_cleanup":["Ordinary driver open/connect errors propagate without automatic rollback; explicit config retry is narrowly scoped.","Disassembly10001d38 PUSH1;10001d42 catch virtual Disconnect/core reconnect;10001d5d PUSH0;100050f7 PUSH1;10005101 catch Disconnect/core reconnect;1000511c PUSH0. Ghidra split tail omitted these pushes; disassembly controls interpretation."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.Disconnect","entries":["0x10001e70","0x10001edc","0x10004390"],"typed_inputs":["noargs"],"ordered_behavior":["StopSyncPeriodicMsg first. If connected: if protocol3 StopSilMsgFilter (exception swallowed by catch-all then continue at1edc); PassThruDisconnect(channelID) result ignored; protocol=0,connected=false,voltage_on=false. ChannelID is NOT zeroed. If opened then PassThruClose(deviceID) ignored; deviceID=0,opened=false. If shimModule nonzero invoke PassThruUnloadLibrary ignored; driverLoadedfalse.","If ownershipworker WaitForSingleObject(handle,0)==WAIT_TIMEOUT102, signal releaseevent, joinINFINITE, set threadfield0. ReleaseOwnership helper is same final ownership-release sequence only."],"errors_cleanup":["Does not explicitly turn off physical programming voltage before clearing voltage flag; no exception translation of ignored close/disconnect/unload errors. No close of ownership threadhandle; events closed only Clear."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.Ownership","entries":["0x10002220","0x10002960","0x10002a60","0x10003730","0x100051b0"],"typed_inputs":["noargs except static thread entry void*"],"ordered_behavior":["HaveOwnership returns immediately if current threadhandle remains WAIT_TIMEOUT. Otherwise lazily create two unnamed manualreset events(acquired@84/release@88); beginthreadex ownership worker; wait any(thread,acquired)INFINITE; resetacquired; if worker is no longer WAIT_TIMEOUT throw CPassThruException2.","Worker creates named ownership mutex TECHSTREAM_MUTEX_J2534 from exported mlptrOWNERSHIP_MUTEX_NAME (DWORD1000d000->100071c0); if NULL simply returns. Attempt Wait0; if not WAIT_OBJECT_0 retry Wait500; only0 treated acquired (abandoned not accepted). On acquired signal acquired event; wait release eventINFINITE; reset releaseevent; ReleaseMutex; CloseHandle(mutex).","Lock/Unlock refers different periodic mutex@54: while periodicthread!=0 wait100 repeatedly until WAIT_OBJECT_0; Unlock ReleaseMutex only if threadfield!=0. No implicit Lock wrapping ordinary WrapRead/WrapWrite."],"errors_cleanup":[],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.SnapshotABI","entries":["0x10002290","0x10002a80"],"typed_inputs":["ExportData(out:typJ2534IF&)","ImportData(in:const typJ2534IF&)"],"ordered_behavior":["Export/Import transport aggregate is native process-local borrowed HANDLE/function-pointer state, NOT serialized wire. offsets typ->object:0->4 deviceID;4->8 boolopened;8->c protocol;c->10 channel;14->14 shimHMODULE;18->18 boolconnected;1c->1c receiveTimeout;20->20 sendTimeout;3c->28 filtercount;40/44->2c/30 filterIDs;48/49->34/35 active;4a->36 voltage;4b->37 padding;4c->80 ownershipthread;50->84 acquired;54->88 release;58->8c MsgDat module;5c->90 snapshot pointer.","typ24/28 are borrowed constchar* device/DLL names on export only when object device exists. Import always allocates fresh CJ2534Device and copies these strings, without destroying previous objectdevice. filtercount copied and iterated unbounded against physical arrays2.","Function-pointer offsets typ60..9c (16DWORDs) map object19c..1d8; typc0 maps object1dc logger-mode. typ10,2c..38,a0..bc unassigned by these routines. Import preserves other ctor state including CANbaud/SILbaud/driverLoaded/snapshot enable rather than copying absent fields."],"errors_cleanup":["Trusts incoming pointers, handles,count and functions; no size/version/bounds validation or refcount/ownership transfer. Writer/prepare/getter receives this exact aggregate from CUW and constructs local object; parent FlashBackend owns production."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.IOControl","entries":["0x10001d80","0x10004540","0x100046a0"],"typed_inputs":["ControlIO(ioctl:u32,in:void*,out:void*)","SetConfigurationParametersForCanFD(direct_bool:bool)","SetProgrammingVoltage(pin:u32,voltage:u32)"],"ordered_behavior":["ControlIO dispatch ID5 first overwrites *(u32*)in=currentprotocol then uses channelID; IDs3,0xe,0x800c use deviceID; allothers channelID. Calls PassThruIoctl with original in/out. Nonzero CJ2534Exception status.","FD config builds SCONFIG_LIST{count5+bool,params*:pairs}:805c=2000000;8001=060e;805d=20; ifbool805e=3;805f=1000;8060=cc; invokes virtual ControlIO(2,configs,NULL). Connect/Switch first pass true (include805e=3), after full reconnect fallback passfalse (omit805e).","ProgrammingVoltage supports ONLY voltagefffffffe (short-to-ground on) if !voltageflag, or ffffffff(off) if flag; every other requested voltage silently no-ops. Calls PassThruSetProgrammingVoltage(deviceID,pin,voltage); nonzero throws, success updates flag."],"errors_cleanup":[],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.Indication","entries":["0x10002590","0x10003950","0x10003a90","0x10003b60","0x10003ba7"],"typed_inputs":["RxStatus:u32","ReadIndication optional prefix:CBytes const& (inline data,length@200,0x408object)","ReadMsgs(out:PASSTHRU_MSG*,count:u32*)"],"ordered_behavior":["GetIndicationFromRxStatus maps RxStatus&0x1f:0=>3,2=>1,9=>0,10=>padding?2:3,others4. ReadIndication() performs one WrapReadMsgs count1 stackmsg then applies map.","ReadIndication(prefix) repeatedly direct PassThruReadMsgs(channel,&stackmsg,&count1,receiveTimeout); resets fields and protocol; any nonzero status throws. Accept candidate iff size>=prefix.length, first4 bytes equal, and if length>=5 fifthbyte equal; only checks atmost5 prefix bytes even if lengthlarger. Discards indication4/unmatched until known.","ReadMsgs calls noarg ReadIndication once and discards its result; catch-all swallows any exception; then WrapReadMsgs(caller buffers,count). Thus an initial successful receive is consumed, and an initial failure does not prevent second read."],"errors_cleanup":[],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.MessageIO","entries":["0x100051c0","0x10005250","0x10005300","0x100053a6","0x10004600","0x10001e60","0x10002210","0x10004510","0x10004690"],"typed_inputs":["PASSTHRU_MSG*:array count inout:u32*","SetCanFramePaddingFlag(bool)","SetPointerOfLastCommunicationMessage(borrowed snapshot*)"],"ordered_behavior":["04message layout 0x1038:protocolu32@0,RxStatusu32@4,TxFlagsu32@8,timestampu32@c,DataSizeu32@10,ExtraDataIndexu32@14,Data[4128]@18. Inline address prefix is caller-owned; layer adds no CAN ID bytes or ISO-TP segmentation. Count/data buffers passed unchanged except mutations below.","WrapRead sets protocol field of EVERY requested slot count before PassThruReadMsgs(channel,msg,count,recvTimeout); status!=0 throws even if partial count/data returned.","WrapWrite overwrites each protocol; protocol6/8012 preserves caller flags and OR40 iff paddingtrue; otherprotocols zero TxFlags. First virtual ControlIO(8,NULL,NULL) clears RXbuffer, throwing if error BEFORE send. Then PassThruWriteMsgs(channel,msg,count,sendTimeout), anynonzero throws, no partial retry.","WriteMsgs snapshots FIRST message before mutation, calls WrapWrite; for6/8012 constructs CBytes first4 data bytes and ReadIndication(prefix), discarding returned indication. Catch-all swallows exceptions from this indication stage (not actual write).","SetLastCommunicationMessage no-op if sinkNULL,enablefalse,or protocol3. sinktype4, or5 iff bit7 in LOW byte of (RxStatus|TxFlags) set; sinklength=DataSize; memcpy entire DataSize from msg+18 to sink+8 without bound check. Setter borrows pointer; enable/disable togglesbyte94; SetPadding togglesbyte37."],"errors_cleanup":["Layer has no UDS negative response/pending parser, block counter, transport retries, cancellation, or max-length gate. Domain helper owners implement NRC78 and protocol predicates."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
  {"id":"FlashTransport.J2534.SpecifiedReads","entries":["0x10003be0","0x10003cfc","0x10003d60","0x10004127","0x10004155","0x10004174","0x10004192","0x1000419f","0x100042ff"],"typed_inputs":["ReadSpecifiedCanMsg(prefix:CBytes&,out:PASSTHRU_MSG*,count:u32*,frame_enum:i32)","ReadSpecifiedCanMsgs(prefixes:std::vector<CBytes>&,out:array PASSTHRU_MSG*,count:u32*)"],"ordered_behavior":["Single: if frameenum1, ReadIndication(prefix) must return1 else throwstatus999; any exception from this indication read is swallowed then converted to999 at10003d18->10003d25. Then repeatedly zero FIRST output msg0x1038, localcount=*count and WrapReadMsgs; accept matching first4bytes (+5th iffprefix.length>4). If frameenum2 additionally accept only RxStatus&1f==0 or10 with paddingfalse. No output-size>=prefix-length predicate here. On accepted set caller count=localcount and snapshot firstmsg. Catch-all read failure sets *count=0 and out.DataSize=0 then rethrows.","Multi: *count=0; zero output n*0x1038; allocate n*0x1038 temp, clone prefix vector. Repeated WrapReadMsgs(max remaining count); for each returned msg compare ENTIRE stored prefix.length (wordwise+tail), accept same data-RxStatus predicate; copy accepted fullmsg to nextoutput, incrementcount, erase ONE matching outstandingprefix, retain duplicate prefixes as separate work. Exit only allprefixes satisfied; unmatched/disallowed discarded. Empty prefix list still enters one zero-count driver read before finish.","Multi exceptions saved by native type: CJ2534Exception and CPassThruException copied/rethrown after freeing temp; unknown exceptions translated CPassThruException9999. Catch-all around read additionally sets *count=0 and firstout.DataSize=0 then rethrows into outer catches. Success snapshots LAST accepted message; no paddingbytes/payload interpretation."],"errors_cleanup":["No total deadline/cancel: each driver read uses current timeout. Prefix length beyond returned DataSize is not bounded by this layer. No collapse of duplicate expected rows."],"typed_results":["void; mutates supplied object/buffers; native exceptions as specified"],"owner":"FlashTransport","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWJ2534DeviceIF.dll"]},
