  {"id":"FlashShared.CEthernetUtils.ThrowConvertedJ2534Exception@0x10002ce0","overload_discriminator_va":"0x10002ce0","source_unit":"flashing.pe.TCUWEthernetUtils.dll","entry_va":"0x10002ce0","export_aliases":[{"ordinal":19,"decorated_typed_abi":"?ThrowConvertedJ2534Exception@CEthernetUtils@@QAEXAAVCWinSockException@@@Z"}],"typed_input_and_result":"public: void __thiscall CEthernetUtils::ThrowConvertedJ2534Exception(class CWinSockException &)","behavior":"Convert WinSock enum2 to CJ2534 code9, every other enum to7; preserve source function/line and throw; no returned status.","evidence_body_id":"FlashShared.TCUWEthernetUtils.internal.10002ce0","implementation_id":"FlashShared.CEthernetUtils.ThrowConvertedJ2534Exception@0x10002ce0","stable_overload_family_id":"FlashShared.CEthernetUtils.ThrowConvertedJ2534Exception","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWEthernetUtils.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.CommonLib.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.commonlib","behavior":["CollectionUtil.IsEmpty<T>(IList<T>) returns true for null or Count==0; TryAdd<K,V> checks ContainsKey and returns false without replacing, otherwise Add then true. TryGet<K,V> returns default(V) for null dictionary/missing key; present key uses indexer.","ConfigurationUtil.GetAppSettings reads ConfigurationManager.AppSettings[key]; absent/empty returns supplied default. int/bool overloads use TryParse and return supplied default on failure, not an exception from parsing.","ConvertUtil.ToInt32(object,int) uses default only for null and otherwise Convert.ToInt32(object), so malformed strings can escape. uint32->int32 and int32->uint32 overloads catch conversion failures and return supplied defaults. These bind CUW numeric status/entity fields and CID arguments, not ECU encoding algorithms.","FileUtil.Combine(string,string[]) folds Path.Combine in input order; Combine(char,string[]) prepends separator to EACH member (including first), not conventional join. File/path/date/XML/collection bodies are fully retained, including exception/finally regions.","CUW uses GetAppSettings for port/service/form settings, TryAdd for static configuration, TryGet for GetConfig, IsEmpty for calibration/report lists, ConvertUtil for native-wrapper status fields; exact argument-producing caller IL is linked by SHA+token+offset."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"CommonLib.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.commonlib","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.CommonLib.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.CryptgraphCommon.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.cryptgraphcommon","behavior":["CUW ConfigReader.ReadConfig(string configPath,string passphrasePath) calls GtsPlus.Tool.Cryptgraph.GtsPlusCM.Decrypt with those two strings, replaces every Editor-header with # Editor-header, then invokes ConfigReader.Parse.","GuiFile/GUI archive cryptography, CM authentication, AES/mask/RSA and hash implementations are retained as actual IL body evidence and delegated to Security; no vehicle session/authentication role is inferred from the assembly name.","All unmanaged declarations (dll, entrypoint, exact signature, import/marshaling flags) are in source_records.pinvoke_bindings. These typed calls join the four GtsPlus-CM native exports, not a generic crypto placeholder."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"CryptgraphCommon.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.cryptgraphcommon","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.CryptgraphCommon.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.CryptgraphResource.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.cryptgraphresource","behavior":["IndividualResource.CreateAuthenticateParams(byte[] challenge,int count)->byte[] initializes exactly16 resource key bytes via RuntimeHelpers.InitializeArray and calls inherited CreateAuthenticateParam(challenge,count,key). Actual FieldRva bytes are pinned in source evidence.","ExtractPassphraseFile()->string fetches resource byte[] ppf_tmc then calls IndividualResourceBase.ExtractFileResource; resource manager is lazily cached, culture is caller-settable. This supplies local packaging authentication material; Security owns its cryptographic interpretation."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"CryptgraphResource.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.cryptgraphresource","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.CryptgraphResource.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.CryptgraphResourceCommon.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.cryptgraphresourcecommon","behavior":["ICryptgraphResource declares string ExtractPassphraseFile() and byte[] CreateAuthenticateParams(byte[],int32). IndividualResourceBase.ExtractFileResource(byte[]) creates temp-path/random-filename, opens FileMode.CreateNew/FileAccess.Write, writes every supplied byte; nested finally disposes BinaryWriter then FileStream and returns path. It does not delete the returned file itself.","CreateAuthenticateParam(byte[] challenge,int count,byte[] key) constructs AesCng, sets KeySize128, CipherMode1(CBC), PaddingMode2(PKCS7), supplied key, encrypts challenge[0:count] with generated IV, returns IV||ciphertext. Security owns algorithm/key resource contract; exact IL delegates rather than ECU assumptions."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"CryptgraphResourceCommon.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.cryptgraphresourcecommon","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.CryptgraphResourceCommon.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.GTSPlusCommon.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.gtspluscommon","behavior":["CryptManagerWrapper PInvokes/authentication/file cryptography and CryptographicFunction.LoadEncryptFile are Security joins. Actual typed native calls, arrays, length arguments, enum conversions and hashes are retained; helper ownership does not move crypto into FlashShared.","IniFileParserFunction.GetKeyDataStringFromFile(section,key,path) calls FileIniDataParser.ReadFile(path)[section][key], maps null/any caught exception to empty string. String-input counterpart parses supplied text then same lookup. Numeric and GetSectionValue<T> bodies retain their exact parsing/reflection gates.","IpcFunction.GetPipeSecurity creates a PipeSecurity and adds Allow PipeAccessRights131487 for SecurityIdentifier(WellKnownSidType1,null), i.e. World SID. AppCommunication pipe constructor consumes this descriptor; no car access control is implied.","SafeList<T> wrappers enter LockObject with Monitor.Enter(ref lockTaken), perform inherited List operation, and release in finally. FixedList.AddFixed appends, if Count>MaxCount removes element0 once, and decrements NextIndex only if positive.","FixedList.GetNextFixed(bool remove) returns default(T) if Count<=0 or Count==NextIndex; else reads at NextIndex and increments it. If remove, decrements index and removes at that same index. GetAllNextFixed repeatedly consumes until boxed result is null; null elements terminate and value-type default does not box to null. Exact behavior is not normalized to a circular-buffer abstraction."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"GTSPlusCommon.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.gtspluscommon","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.GTSPlusCommon.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.GTSPlusErrorReportData.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.errorreportdata","behavior":["DTO get_/set_ bodies directly access typed backing fields. Full declarations/signatures and every actual body preserve report vehicle/PC/process/action/communication/status data, rather than inventing a vehicle transport format.","ObjectConverter<T>.ToByteArray serializes boxed value using BinaryFormatter into MemoryStream then ToArray; FromByteArray deserializes MemoryStream(bytes), unbox.any T; finally disposes streams. BinaryFormatter framing is process IPC/persistence, not ECU packets.","WriteObject<T>(BinaryWriter,T,bool encrypt) serializes, optionally delegates Encrypt, prepends BitConverter.GetBytes(int32 payloadLength), concatenates bytes, writes byte[]. Current supported Windows little-endian produces4-byte LE length. No extra message type/CRC is added by this helper.","ReadObject<T>(BinaryReader,bool decrypt) reads signed ReadInt32 length; while nonzero reads chunks min(remaining,65535), allocates full chunk, calls BinaryReader.Read once and discards returned count, appends full array, subtracts requested chunk. Therefore short reads retain zero-filled suffix; there is no retry/exact-read loop or declared size cap. Zero length proceeds to BinaryFormatter on empty array; negative length reaches invalid array allocation. Optional Decrypt then FromByteArray. Exceptions propagate from this helper.","Encrypt/Decrypt and pipe key/IV constants delegate Security; caller bool flags and typed payloads are preserved in MsgDatComm bodies.","InternalLog.Output serializes writers with mutex Global\\ER_InternalLogOutput; fills UTC timestamp components from a captured local DateTime, nullable parameters, process main module (empty on failure), and text. Directory is CommonApplicationData(46)\\GTSPlus Common\\ErrorReport. Uses invariant-culture CsvWriter with UTF8Encoding(false). New-file header always quoted; data quote predicate is WritingContext.Record.Count in{7,9,13}. Appends newest matching daily file only when length<1048576; otherwise creates int_yyyyMMddHHmmssfff.log. On new file removes descending-name entries after newest10. Nested finally disposes writer/stream, releases/disposes mutex; outer catch suppresses logging failures."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"GTSPlusErrorReportData.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.errorreportdata","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.GTSPlusErrorReportData.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.GtsPlus-CM.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.native-cm-boundary","behavior":["Exact recovered native exports are CreateChallengeCode RVA0x1e70, CheckAuthenticationCode RVA0x1f70, DoFileEncryption RVA0x2540, DoFileDecryption RVA0x2aa0. Managed PInvoke declarations/callers in CryptgraphCommon and GTSPlusCommon define array/pointer/string/int32 argument/result bindings. SecurityFlashCrypto owns native bodies and every cryptographic branch; this support section does not reclassify them as ECU seed/key algorithms."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"GtsPlus-CM.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.native-cm-boundary","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.GtsPlus-CM.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.MsgDatComm.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.msgdatcomm","behavior":["Provides application/error-report named pipes on local machine dot, not vehicle communication. All ER methods and seven async MoveNext bodies are included with exact labels, callback signatures, payload DTOs, constants, EH paths and typed calls.","ER_StartApplicationCS(string resultCode)->int32 builds ApplicationStartData(resultCode,currentProcessId), opens ER_ApplicationStart in PipeDirection.Out, Connect(1 ms), WriteObject(encrypt:true), Flush, WaitForPipeDrain, disposes writer then pipe; returns1. Catch logs diagnostic ResultCode26 then returns0 (26 is not its return). ER_EndApplicationCS similarly sends ApplicationEndData(processId) to ER_ApplicationEnd, catch diagnostic8 then0.","Action/communication logs, log settings, error reporting, application messages, pull operations and running status queries use the explicit pipe names in per-method contracts. The methods returning int32 generally expose success1/failure0 while logged diagnostic enum numbers differ; exact return/control-flow IL is authoritative for each method.","Alive-monitor start rejects nonnull existing task; otherwise creates CancellationTokenSource and starts AliveMonitorAsync(name,callback). Stop rejects no task; otherwise Cancel, Task.Wait, clear task. Ending start rejects nonempty task list then starts ConfirmEndingAsync and ExecuteEndingAsync sharing cancellation source. Ending stop Cancel then Clear WITHOUT waiting for tasks. Error-wait stop uses Cancel, Task.WhenAll(...).Wait, Clear. AppCommunication stop Cancel, Wait, clear task. Do not conflate these shutdown orderings.","Async server names are ER_AliveMonitor_+name, ER_EndingConfirm_+name, ER_EndingExecute_+name, ER_AppCommunicationResponse+name; error/dialog servers use fixed names. WaitForConnectionAsync uses cancellation token and ConfigureAwait(false); callback/payload read/write/disconnect/repeat and cancellation catches are retained in state-machine IL.","ER_CreateChallengeCodeCS and ER_CheckAutorizationCodeCS, ChallengeCode and AuthenticateStatus are local DLL authorization delegated Security. PullLogOperation checks authorization; other method gates are body-specific, not a blanket DLL gate."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"MsgDatComm.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.msgdatcomm","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.MsgDatComm.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.MsgDatCommWrapper.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.msgdatcommwrapper","behavior":["Native export ER_SetCommunicationLogModeCS RVA0x1180 is six bytes ff2500e00010 (jmp [VA0x1000e000]); CLR VTableFixups points slot RVA0xe000 to MethodDef0x06000001. This is a CLR export bridge, not a transport implementation.","MethodDef0x06000001 returns int32 and accepts int32 mode (C++/CLI modopts retained). Allocates C++ exception record, constructs MsgDatComm.CExternalMethod, initializes result0, calls instance ER_SetCommunicationLogModeCS(mode), returns its result. Native C++ catch filter/register/unregister handling preserves result0 on handled exception; rethrow path is retained. Body192 bytes SHA1472f857d2437f462c7ec76a0133c2fbfcefd11f0b7a0397c4a9c80ed89d0170.","The managed target Enum.ToObject casts mode into OutputModeType (no range validation), assigns CommunicationLogOutputSettingData.OutputMode, sends encrypted frame to ER_CommunicationLogOutputSetting on local pipe with Connect(1), Flush/WaitForPipeDrain/dispose; success1 and catch0. Remaining wrapper methods are C++/CLI CRT/module-domain initialization and unwind scaffolding, retained as bodies/native declarations, not vehicle algorithms."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"MsgDatCommWrapper.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.msgdatcommwrapper","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.MsgDatCommWrapper.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.Newtonsoft.JsonWrapper.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.jsonwrapper","behavior":["Only application method CJSONWrapper.SerializeObject(object value,bool indented)->string branches bool to Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting0(None)/1(Indented), calls JsonConvert.SerializeObject(object,Formatting), returns result, no catch/settings/retries.","Actual caller TCUWVehicleInfoUpdateFileWriter.CVehicleInfoUpdateFileWriter.ExportFile(char*,_typVehicleInfo*,format)->bool rejects already-existing output file, creates directory, chooses CManagedVehicleInfo for format==1 else CManagedVehicleInfoForAISAC2, calls wrapper with true, writes UTF8Encoding(false) with append=false, Flush, marks success; finally closes writer. C++ EH returns false for handled write failures. Vehicle fields/conversion belong the file-writer owner; serializer contributes no ECU payload algorithm."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"Newtonsoft.JsonWrapper.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.jsonwrapper","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.Newtonsoft.JsonWrapper.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.CsvHelper.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.csvhelper","behavior":["Actual canonical uses are internal/error-report CSV logging, not flashing bus I/O. Bindings include CsvWriter(TextWriter,CultureInfo), get_Configuration/set_ShouldQuote, WriteHeader<LogCSVData>, WriteRecord<T>, NextRecord, Flush/Dispose and WritingContext.Record. 221 invoked/name-matched implementation bodies retained including generic/async overloads; interface declaration is distinguished from concrete implementation.","GTSPlusErrorReportData.InternalLog.Output supplies invariant culture, UTF8 no BOM, explicit quote callbacks; Index attributes and typed LogCSVData setters determine column data. ErrorReport.DoubleBufferLogTask.TempSave callers are source-qualified in canonical_caller_bodies. No CSV retry/validation policy is invented in FlashShared."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"CsvHelper.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.csvhelper","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.CsvHelper.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.Fleck.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.fleck","behavior":["CUW Init constructs WebSocketServer(url), sets EnabledSslProtocols3072(TLS1.2) and certificate. Start starts local timer, calls server.Start(OnClientConnect), changes status2; Stop requires initialized clientPool then status1, clears pool, stops timer, disposes server and invokes OnShutdown.","OnClientConnect logs endpoint/id, closes unless service IsRunning, then closes if ConnectionCount>=MaxConnection, else creates ClientConnection/ClientSession, subscribes OnClose and adds pool. ClientConnection caches GUID string session id and installs OnClose/OnError/OnMessage/OnBinary callbacks.","ClientConnection.Send(string) calls IWebSocketConnection.Send(string)->Task and POPs the returned Task; asynchronous send errors are not awaited here. Disconnect checks IsAvailable before Close. Concrete Fleck Send requires nonnull handler (otherwise InvalidOperationException), returns faulted Task when closing/unavailable, otherwise frames text/binary and SendBytes. Close() uses code1000, sets closing and either closes socket immediately or frames close then closes after send.","Concrete WebSocketServer.Start binds configured IPEndPoint, Listen backlog100, updates actual port; wss with no certificate logs and returns (does not throw here); zero TLS setting would default192 but CUW supplies3072; calls ListenForClients and stores config callback. Dispose disposes ListenerSocket. These are local browser/API transport semantics, not ECU diagnostics."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"Fleck.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.fleck","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.Fleck.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.GTSPluscoree32.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.coree32","behavior":["Shipped x86 _CorExeMain RVA0x1000 executes three-byte-path jmp0x1003; jmp0x1007; ret (prefixeb0168eb025968c3); EAX is unassigned by this path. Linear decoding across skipped fake push opcodes is wrong.","DllMain(module,reason,reserved)->BOOL initializes target0; only PROCESS_ATTACH(reason1), CompatibleOS()==true and command line NOT ending UTF16 CRLFCRLF invokes ReadOriginalExeEntryPoint. If nonzero target, calls it as no-argument function pointer, ignores result. Always returnsTRUE on normal return; faults/exception from target are not caught.","CompatibleOS loads existing ntdll.dll via GetModuleHandleA (does not LoadLibrary), manually resolves nonforwarded RtlGetVersion, zeroes284-byte RTL_OSVERSIONINFOEXW with size284. Requires NTSTATUS>=0, unsigned major>=5, excludes major5/minor0. Missing module/export/failing status return0. Resolver validates MZ/PE and nonzero NumberOfRvaAndSizes/exportRVA/exportSize, scans names and ordinal indexes, rejects null and forwarded exports; no forwarded resolution/array bounds hardening.","ReadOriginalExeEntryPoint obtains current EXE path into260WCHAR, opens GENERIC_READ/FILE_SHARE_READ/OPEN_EXISTING with flags0, reads exactly4096 bytes into static bufferRVA0x301c, closes valid handle even on read failure. Failure/short read=>target0. Successful read validates MZ/PE through helper then reads AddressOfEntryPoint at NT+0x28; nonzero becomes (uint32)GetModuleHandleA(NULL)+RVA. GetModuleFileNameW return and NT-helper null are NOT checked; malformed/truncated header may fault. e_lfanew/entry RVA have no file/image bounds checks.","Command-line suffix check uses wcslen and exact last4 code units13,10,13,10, false for length<4. It gates calling the executable original entrypoint, not an ECU/security session. Manual C-like lifts, complete control-flow instruction bytes/hashes and exact source bytes are included; no application/native execution occurred."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"GTSPluscoree32.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.coree32","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.GTSPluscoree32.dll"]},
  {"unit_id":"flashing.pe.GTSPluscoree64.dll","contract_id":"flashshared.support.coree64","behavior":["Shipped x64 _CorExeMain RVA0x1330 calls leafRVAs1010/1020 then tailjumps1000, effective return0x110(272). Marker leafRVAs1000..1070 return0x110/111/112/113/120/121/122/123 without memory writes.","DllMain(module,reason,reserved)->BOOL only PROCESS_ATTACH computes target, using always-supported gateRVA0x1310=>1 and same UTF16 CRLFCRLF suffix exclusion; nonzero original EXE entrypoint is called with no explicit arguments, result ignored. Normal returnTRUE; no managed/ECU operation is invoked by the export itself. Marker calls are retained in instruction evidence and have no state.","LoaderRVA0x11a0 uses same260WCHAR path, GENERIC_READ/FILE_SHARE_READ/OPEN_EXISTING, exact4096-byte read and CloseHandle sequence as x86, static bufferRVA0x30f0. MZ/PE helperRVA0x1140 signextends e_lfanew; loader signextends int32 AddressOfEntryPoint at NT+0x28 when adding loaded EXE base. Missing/short read or zeroEP=>target0; no path-result/header-helper-null/offset bounds checks. Stack cookie is checked atRVA1490; mismatch dispatches failure handler rather than an ECU error result.","Unlike x86 there is NO RtlGetVersion/export resolver compatibility check; gate always1. All branch/cleanup/failure behavior follows byte-pinned manual lifts and CFG evidence; original entrypoint effects belong that executable. No real Windows/client/native execution was performed."],"transitive_runtime_bindings":[],"native_import_bindings_ref":{"artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","collection":"native_import_bindings","library":"GTSPluscoree64.dll"},"id":"flashshared.support.coree64","owner":"FlashShared","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.GTSPluscoree64.dll"]},
