  {"id":"FlashWritersB.StreamedSource","record_input":"typSFormatRecord stride16: u8type@0,u32address@4,u32length@8,data*@12. Memory backing record list at+14,count+18; raw buffer at+0,size+4; file flag+1c.","memory":"If no record list use backing buffer and backing.size, NOT UDS-declared length. Else malloc declared source length; call FlashShared.CUnifiedUtils.MakeSendData(records,count,numericAddress,declaredSourceLength,out), then send that length. Shared helper copies whole qualifying records, skips firstS1, can overrun or leave bytes uninitialized; caller performs no coverage/truncation check. Free scratch buffer on success/unwind.","block":"ceil(sourceLen/payloadMax), last=min(payloadMax,remaining),36||u8seq||data; seq initially1 for EACH area; increment u8 only after successful block, wraps255->0. Expected76||sameSeq and minimum framing+2. Each block catches ONLY CJ2534Exception raw status+2c in{9,16}, retry at most2 times (3 total sends); identical data/sequence and offset retained. Any other code or exhausted budget rethrows. Offset/CPU completed increment only after success.","progress":"total/completed vectors u32 sized imported glngNUM_CPU_MAXNUM. For logicalIndex0 and completed<=firstRoutineByteCount no UI updates. BytesCPU=truncate((double(u32completed)/double(u32total))*signedCPUImageSize). PercentCPU=logicalIndex0 ? truncate(100*double(u32(completed-firstRoutine))/double(u32(total-firstRoutine))) : truncate(100*double(completed)/double(total)). Writes borrowed arrays, callbacks+28/+2c with context. Unsigned subtractions wrap; zero denominators not guarded; no UI clamp. callbacks+70(context,logicalIndex) before each logical block and callback+4(context) between differing CPU indexes.","binary_file":"fstream binary open(flags0x21,sharing0x40), path descriptor+4, seek descriptor+114, endInclusive descriptor+10c. TargetCompleted=entryCompleted+declaredSourceLength. malloc5MiB, zero whole buffer each read. Require gcount==requested min(5MiB,end-position+1), else error9999. Send whole payloadMax chunks; rewind partial remainder for next read. If short read<max, send min(targetRemaining,max) with read bytes followed by zero padding where needed. If file ends before target, send zero-filled chunks until target. Require completed==target else9999. Close and free on success/unwind; close failure sets stream failure state. No file hash or signature check in this loop.","srecord_parser":"Require S + type0/1/2/3/5/7/8/9. Width(address+checksum)=3 for0/1/5/9,4 for2/8,5 for3/7. Hex count atchars2,3 must>=width, recordchars=4+2*count; insufficientbuffer returns2. Both ASCII cases and0-9 accepted; invalid hex throwsCPassThruException0x3f7, structure/checksum throws0x3f6. S1/2/3 addresses BE16/24/32; data count=count-width. S7/8/9 require count==width. S5 decodes record-count field width based on count chars and compares to seen data record count only mode0; writer uses mode1. Checksum requires low8(count+address+data+checksum)==255. Returns consumed chars plus up to2 CR/LF; return1 exact buffer exhaustion,0 when bytes remain. mode1 exposes ASCII data span for later hex decoding; does not cryptographically verify. S5 decodedcount3/4/5 selectsBE16/24/32 recordcount respectively;othercount encodings error0x3f6. Record-countcomparisononlymode0;writersusemode1.","srecord_stream":"malloc5MiB+1 input and payloadMax output. Match requested numeric address against variant descriptor maps; unknown address error9999. Mapped filepos0 means zero-fill mode without opening file. Nonzero path opens as binary and seeks. Exact gcount required. Parse mode1; carry/reseek incomplete record across refill, repeated incomplete parse error9999. First relevant data address below requested address errors9999. Decode complete record data to current output block; if current bytes+record bytes>payloadMax throw9999 rather than splitting that record to fit. Clamp appended bytes to remaining declared target. Send full block or terminal partial block. On file exhaustion close and zero-fill remainder to target. Require completed==target. All files/buffers closed/freed on normal/unwind. Original S-record addresses choose initial mapping/first-record admissibility; remaining record data is concatenated, not a sparse address-driven MakeSendData call.","typed_joins":[{"contract_id":"FlashShared.CUnifiedUtils.MakeSendData","implementation_id":"FlashShared.CUnifiedUtils.MakeSendData@0x10004360","artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","ABI":"static void __cdecl(const typSFormatRecord*,u32 count,u32 minimum,u32 requested,char*out)"},{"contract_id":"backend.calibration.repro-method-classification","artifact":"source-bound raw/typed evidence","ABI":"GetReproMethodType(CLogicalBlockInfo const&)->0unknown/1whole/2delta/3compression"}],"owner":"FlashWritersB","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCanSuzukiUSBReproUDSFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCanUnifiedFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWCanUnifiedFlashWriterEachArea.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWEthernetReprostdFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanAirbagFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanBodyFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanBodyFlashWriterForCXPI.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanChassisShrinkFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanClearanceSonarFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanDSS1FlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanSecurityAirbagFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanSecurityChassisShrinkFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP4CanVFORESTFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP5CanBodyFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP5CanDHUDSFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWP6CanReprostdFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWSilDCMPRLFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWSilFlashWriter.dll","cuw_utility.flash-pe.TCUWSilHINOFlashWriterForAMT.dll"]},
