  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.getRequestReprogrammingKeyByOffline","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-224-getRequestReprogrammingKeyByOffline","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"getRequestReprogrammingKeyByOffline","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-224-getRequestReprogrammingKeyByOffline","prototype_index":224,"name":"getRequestReprogrammingKeyByOffline","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[220475,221762],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["faultMsg","isReturn"],"state":["model.repsecRetryCnt","model.statusOfReprogramming.cpuInfos","model.pathOfXmlFileForOffline","CONFIG_KEY_CAN_OFFLINE_REPSEC"],"ordered_transitions":["Increment repsecRetryCnt only when isReturn === false.","Compute isExistsEnd = isExistsEndProgress(cpuInfos) && repsecRetryCnt < 3.","Read CONFIG_KEY_CAN_OFFLINE_REPSEC. Convert config.value and showS701112(isExistsEnd,canOffline,faultMsg).","Cancel logs the operation and calls cancelingReprogramming(). If it returns Cancel, recurse with (faultMsg,true).","Offline logs the operation. Set saveXml according to pathOfXmlFileForOffline === undefined. Return readSignature(S701-112,saveXml,faultMsg).","Every other choice logs Retry and returns getRequestReprogrammingKeyByAuto()."],"request_response":["model.getConfigParam(CONFIG_KEY_CAN_OFFLINE_REPSEC) -> config.value","showS701112(isExistsEnd,canOffline,faultMsg) -> {clicked}"],"errors":["No local catch. Configuration, view, and delegated failures propagate.","The count < 3 changes the view argument. This method does not enforce a hard retry stop."],"visible":["S701112 and delegated cancellation/offline screens"],"mutations":["repsecRetryCnt increment","repro logs"],"cancellation":["Refused cancellation returns to S701112 without incrementing repsecRetryCnt."],"cleanup":["No local cleanup."],"promise":"Returns the configuration chain and adopts each selected branch.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.readSignature","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-225-readSignature","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"readSignature","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-225-readSignature","prototype_index":225,"name":"readSignature","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[221762,225977],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["backTo","saveXml","faultMsg"],"state":["model.pathOfXmlFileForOffline","CONFIG_KEY_DOCUMENT_FOLDER","model.calCount","model.statusOfReprogramming","controller.currentView"],"ordered_transitions":["Define backFunc by backTo. For S701-110, log S701-87 Back and show S701110 again.","In that S701110 branch, Cancel calls cancelingReprogramming(). A returned Cancel restarts automatic selection. Offline calls readSignature(backTo,false,undefined).","For backTo === S701-112, Back logs the operation and returns getRequestReprogrammingKeyByOffline(faultMsg,true). Other backTo values leave backFunc undefined.","Define the file chooser with option={filter:[xml],localeId:gts.util.getLocaleFormat()}. Create FileDialogController(commonInfo,option), call init(), read CONFIG_KEY_DOCUMENT_FOLDER, then call showDialog(result.value).","On S70187 Next, log Next. Show the chooser. A resolved chooser logs S701-12 Open and enters loadXmlFunc.","For result with fileName !== null and fileName.length > 0, form requestKeyFile=result.directory + backslash + result.fileName.","Initialize S70185, then call loadXMLFileForReprogrammingKey(requestKeyFile). On returnValue === SUCCESS, initialize S70117(calCount).","After S70117 initialization, call controller.updateS70117() if statusOfReprogramming exists. Return monitoringReprogrammingStatus().","For a non-SUCCESS load result, show S70179. Yes logs Yes, calls informResultOfQueryRetry(CuwModel.Retry.RETRY), then recurses with saveXml=false.","S70179 non-Yes logs No, then shows S70100. S70100 No recurses with saveXml=false. Every other choice logs Yes, cancels the key request, then shows S70181.","For an empty chooser result, restore currentView buttons. The chooser-chain catch also logs S701-12 Cancel and restores buttons.","Initially, saveXml === true calls saveXMLFileForRequestReprogrammingKey(). Otherwise create {requestKeyFile:model.pathOfXmlFileForOffline}.","Create ViewS70187. Bind NEXT to nextFunc and BACK to backFunc. Replace the view and return init(result.requestKeyFile)."],"request_response":["model.saveXMLFileForRequestReprogrammingKey() -> {requestKeyFile}","model.getConfigParam(CONFIG_KEY_DOCUMENT_FOLDER) -> {value}","fileDialog.showDialog(documentFolder) -> {directory,fileName}","model.loadXMLFileForReprogrammingKey(directory + backslash + fileName) -> {returnValue}","model.informResultOfQueryRetry(CuwModel.Retry.RETRY) -> ignored result","viewS70187.init(result.requestKeyFile)"],"errors":["The chooser-chain catch also catches load, progress-init, monitoring, and S70179-chain rejections. It labels these as chooser Cancel and restores buttons.","Initial XML-save and S70187-init failures propagate through the returned promise. No outer catch exists.","The file guard does not test fileName === undefined before reading fileName.length. Such an error reaches the chooser-chain catch."],"visible":["S70187 request XML path","FileDialogController xml filter","S70185","S70117","S70179 retry dialog","S70100 cancel confirmation","S70181"],"mutations":["XML save/load delegate to the model","currentView.restoreBtn() on chooser/load-chain failure","repro logs"],"cancellation":["Back returns to the selected security screen. File chooser cancellation restores buttons.","Confirmed S70100 cancellation calls cancelRequestReprogrammingKey() before S70181."],"cleanup":["View replacement delegates to disposeSettingView. No local event removal."],"promise":"Returns the initial save/reuse-and-view-init chain. Later event callback promises do not extend that initial promise.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.cancelingReprogramming","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-226-cancelingReprogramming","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"cancelingReprogramming","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-226-cancelingReprogramming","prototype_index":226,"name":"cancelingReprogramming","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[225977,226618],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":[],"state":["controller.viewReprogramCuw"],"ordered_transitions":["Show S70100.","If clicked === Yes, log Yes. Return cancelRequestReprogrammingKey(), then showS70181().","For every other choice, log No and return Promise.resolve(Cancel)."],"request_response":["view.showDialogS70100() -> {clicked}","cancelRequestReprogrammingKey() -> ignored result"],"errors":["No local catch. Dialog or cancellation failures propagate."],"visible":["S70100 confirmation","S70181 after confirmed cancellation"],"mutations":["repro logs"],"cancellation":["Cancel is a return sentinel for refusing cancellation. A confirmed cancellation has no explicit return sentinel."],"cleanup":["No local cleanup."],"promise":"Returns the dialog chain and adopts the cancellation/quit chain.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.doReprogrammingWithIgOff","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-227-doReprogrammingWithIgOff","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"doReprogrammingWithIgOff","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-227-doReprogrammingWithIgOff","prototype_index":227,"name":"doReprogrammingWithIgOff","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[226618,227232],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":[],"state":["model.batteryVoltage","controller.viewReprogramCuw (bound but unused)"],"ordered_transitions":["Call model.getBatteryVoltage().","If isJ2534ErrStatus(result.returnValue), call checkJ2534StatusAfterConnect(returnValue,doReprogrammingWithIgOff.bind(controller)). Do not return that call.","Otherwise set model.batteryVoltage=result.batteryVoltage and return showS701115()."],"request_response":["model.getBatteryVoltage() -> {returnValue,batteryVoltage}","checkJ2534StatusAfterConnect(result.returnValue,retryCallback)"],"errors":["The returned chain catch logs the error and returns Promise.reject(err).","An asynchronous J2534-handler failure is not joined because its return value is discarded."],"visible":["S701115 or delegated J2534 recovery UI"],"mutations":["model.batteryVoltage on the non-J2534 branch"],"cancellation":["No local cancel listener."],"cleanup":["No local cleanup."],"promise":"Returns the battery-request chain. showS701115() itself returns undefined.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.showS701115","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-228-showS701115","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"showS701115","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-228-showS701115","prototype_index":228,"name":"showS701115","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[227232,228336],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":[],"state":["model.isStartReprogramming","model.batteryVoltage","CONFIG_KEY_BATT_VOL_THRESHOLD"],"ordered_transitions":["Set model.isStartReprogramming=false.","Define Start to set isStartReprogramming=true and request battery voltage again.","Start routes a J2534 error to checkJ2534StatusAfterConnect(returnValue,doReprogrammingWithIgOff.bind(controller)). Otherwise call onClickS70115StartBtn(controller,{}).","Define Cancel to call onClickS70114CancelBtn(controller,{}).","Read CONFIG_KEY_BATT_VOL_THRESHOLD. Create ViewS701115 and bind START/CANCEL.","Replace the current view. Call viewS701115.init(model.batteryVoltage,batteryLowerLimit).","After init resolves, call recursiveCheckShowS701115(controller,viewS701115,batteryLowerLimit,empty string)."],"request_response":["model.getConfigParam(CONFIG_KEY_BATT_VOL_THRESHOLD) -> batteryLowerLimit object","model.getBatteryVoltage() -> {returnValue}","viewS701115.init(model.batteryVoltage,batteryLowerLimit)"],"errors":["No catch exists for the config/init chain or the Start battery request.","Start does not save the fresh batteryVoltage or inspect low/high voltage codes unless isJ2534ErrStatus classifies them."],"visible":["ViewS701115"],"mutations":["model.isStartReprogramming=false at entry","model.isStartReprogramming=true before the Start request"],"cancellation":["CANCEL delegates to onClickS70114CancelBtn(controller,{})."],"cleanup":["View replacement only. No timer handle exists here."],"promise":"Returns undefined. Config, init, and Start requests run in separate internal chains.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.recursiveCheckShowS701115","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-229-recursiveCheckShowS701115","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"recursiveCheckShowS701115","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-229-recursiveCheckShowS701115","prototype_index":229,"name":"recursiveCheckShowS701115","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[228336,230400],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["controller","viewS701115","batteryLowerLimit","logCheckVal"],"state":["model.isStartReprogramming","model.canExecuteS70115","model.batteryVoltage","CuwModel.TimerInterval"],"ordered_transitions":["If isStartReprogramming is truthy, return immediately without scheduling another check.","If canExecuteS70115 is false, schedule this method after CuwModel.TimerInterval with unchanged arguments.","Otherwise request battery voltage. Compare result.returnValue with logCheckVal to select the log-output flag. Replace local logCheckVal with returnValue.","A J2534 error calls checkJ2534StatusAfterConnect(returnValue,callback calling doReprogrammingWithIgOff()). Do not schedule another local timer.","BATTERY_VOLTAGE_IS_BELOW_STANDARD saves batteryVoltage and refreshes S701115. Show S70138 with doReprogrammingWithIgOff.bind(controller).","BATTERY_VOLTAGE_IS_ABOVE_STANDARD saves batteryVoltage and refreshes S701115. Show S701104(result.batteryVoltageUpperThreshold,retryCallback).","Every other returnValue saves batteryVoltage and refreshes S701115. Schedule another check after CuwModel.TimerInterval, carrying logCheckVal."],"request_response":["model.getBatteryVoltage() -> {returnValue,batteryVoltage,batteryVoltageUpperThreshold}","viewS701115.refreshS701115(model.batteryVoltage)"],"errors":["Battery-request or synchronous callback rejection logs an error and calls showS70181().","J2534 and low/high dialog calls are not returned into the chain. Their asynchronous failures do not reach this catch."],"visible":["S701115 voltage refresh","S70138 low voltage","S701104 high voltage","delegated J2534 recovery","S70181 on error"],"mutations":["model.batteryVoltage on low/high/normal branches","local logCheckVal"],"cancellation":["isStartReprogramming is the sole local stop guard. No cancel event is wired here."],"cleanup":["The method does not save timeout handles or clear a previously scheduled timeout."],"promise":"Returns undefined on all normal branches. The battery-request chain is not returned.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.showS701116","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-230-showS701116","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"showS701116","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-230-showS701116","prototype_index":230,"name":"showS701116","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[230400,231373],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["userErrCode"],"state":["controller.model","controller.viewReprogramCuw"],"ordered_transitions":["Create ViewS701116. Bind CANCEL to onClickS70144CancelBtn(controller).","Bind RETRY to model.informResultOfQueryRetry(CuwModel.Retry.RETRY).","After retry acknowledgement, log S701-116 Retry and call checkJ2534StatusAfterConnect(result.returnValue,doReprogrammingWithIgOff.bind(controller)).","Replace the current view. Call init(userErrCode).","After init resolves, show S701117. After its promise resolves, append S701-117 OK without checking a clicked field."],"request_response":["model.informResultOfQueryRetry(CuwModel.Retry.RETRY) -> {returnValue}","viewS701116.init(userErrCode)","view.showDialogS701117() -> result ignored"],"errors":["No local catch for init, retry, or S701117. The J2534 handler is not returned into the retry chain."],"visible":["ViewS701116","S701117 after init"],"mutations":["repro logs"],"cancellation":["CANCEL delegates to onClickS70144CancelBtn(controller)."],"cleanup":["Only delegated view replacement."],"promise":"Returns undefined. Both the init/dialog chain and retry chain are internal.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.writeVehicleInformationForAisac2","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-231-writeVehicleInformationForAisac2","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"writeVehicleInformationForAisac2","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-231-writeVehicleInformationForAisac2","prototype_index":231,"name":"writeVehicleInformationForAisac2","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[231373,242853],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["filePath","ecuGrpList","vinNo"],"state":["model.commonInfo","surrogate ECU groups","model.isSendVehicleInfoForDH","ECU IDs 498(front camera),459(telematics),6064/6564(P6 telematics),476(ADS),636(DH gateway),610(DH meter)"],"ordered_transitions":["Create the AISAC2 json envelope and empty frontCamInfo, telematicsInfo, telematicsInfoP6, dhMeterInfo, ads, and ecuDataList.","Search groups in order for the first ecuInfo with ecuId === 636. If found, call isSendVehicleForDHCGW(ecuGrpList). Reject if model.isSendVehicleInfoForDH is falsy.","Get model.getSurrogateEcuList(). Call mergeEquippedEcuList(ecuGrpList,surrogateEcuGrp).","Build one sequential promise chain across all groups and their ECU entries, in iteration order.","For a surrogate ECU, synthesize {apiArgs:{connect:1}}. Otherwise call checkEcuConnect(ecuGrpId,ecuId,busId). Skip each ECU unless result.apiArgs.connect === 1.","For connected ECUs, set installed flags for ADS, camera, telematics, P6 telematics, and DH meter. The first matching P6 ECU supplies telematicsInfoP6.ecuId and busId.","Create a fresh ecuData record with the exact read flags, buffers, metadata, and isSurrogate defaults in payload_shapes.ecuData_initializer.","For a surrogate, copy addressType and diagAddress. Append ecuData to ecuDataList, then call model.getEcuInfo(ecuData).","After collection, call requestSecurityAccessForAds() only when hasAds. If no ADS, resolve this stage.","For ADS result.dialog === 121, show S701121 and log OK. Call transitSession(1), then endGeneralComm(), then reject.","For ADS result.dialog === 122, call transitSession(1), then endGeneralComm(). Show S701122 and log Next.","Then show S70143 with dispTime=10 and a 1000 ms interval. Each tick first checks value > dispTime, then updates progress(++value).","On that condition, clear the interval and resolve its deferred. The condition first succeeds on tick 12, which also updates progress to 12.","Show S701123 and log Next. Wait 5000 ms. Call releaseVim(), then readSwinForAds(ads). Other ADS dialog values add no operation.","Next, in this exact order, conditionally read camera SWIN, P5 telematics time, P6 telematics time, and DH meter time.","The calls are readSwinFromFrontCam(frontCamInfo), readTimeInformationP5(telematicsInfo), readTimeInformationP6(telematicsInfoP6), readTimeInformationForDHMeter(dhMeterInfo).","Filter ecuDataList. Phase 4 requires validReadEcuPartNumberForPhase4 && validGetCid && (isSuccessSendMessage52 || isSuccessGetCid).","Every other phase requires validReadEcuPartNumber && validReadSoftwarePartNumber && (isSuccessSendMessage8 || isSuccessSendMessage9).","Get writtenCids=getCidListForWriteFlg(). For each retained ECU, create a parent record using the exact output shape.","Map commConfig.address to addressType and diagAddress using payload_rules.address_mapping. A surrogate then overrides both values.","Use cameraSwin only for ecuId 498 with frontCamInfo.cameraReadSwin truthy. Otherwise use ads.adsSwin only for ecuId 476 with ads.adsSwin truthy. Default SWIN is empty.","Append one {swin} entry to parent.swinList. If swNoNum !== 1, create one child per subPartInfo.","Each child inherits parent ecuAssyNo, address, and swinList. Its hardware uses childInfo.hwPartNo. Its serial uses childInfo.serialNo then parent.serialNo.","Each child uses childInfo.swNoList by reference. Its cBest is [{cBestData:empty string}].","For each swNo at index, find subPartInfo entries with the greatest positive count <= index+1. Keep every tie at that greatest count.","If such entries exist, append {swNo,writeFlg:0} to each child whose hwPartNo matches any selected entry. Otherwise append it to the parent.","If any parent/child swNoList is empty, append {swNo:empty string,writeFlg:0}.","Exclude a parent/child only when hwPartNo === empty string and every swNo is null or empty string. Append all other records to reqData.ecuInfo.","For every appended software entry, assign writeFlg=1 if writtenCids.includes(swNo), otherwise 0. Both values are strings.","Choose both time fields from the first object with truthy dcmLocalWriteTime: P5 telematics, then P6 telematics, then DH meter.","If none supplies time, leave dcmLocalWriteTime empty. Set localWriteTime to new Date().toISOString().slice(0,-5) + Z.","Set reqData.ifHash=model.createHash(json), then call model.writeFile(filePath,json)."],"request_response":["model.isSendVehicleForDHCGW(ecuGrpList) -> reads model.isSendVehicleInfoForDH","model.checkEcuConnect(ecuGrpId,ecuId,busId) -> {apiArgs:{connect}}","model.getEcuInfo(ecuData) -> mutates ecuData","model.requestSecurityAccessForAds() -> {dialog}","model.transitSession(1), model.endGeneralComm(), model.releaseVim() -> ignored results","model.readSwinForAds(ads), model.readSwinFromFrontCam(frontCamInfo), model.readTimeInformationP5(telematicsInfo), model.readTimeInformationP6(telematicsInfoP6), model.readTimeInformationForDHMeter(dhMeterInfo) -> mutate supplied objects","model.getCidListForWriteFlg() -> software identifiers","model.createHash(json) -> reqData.ifHash","model.writeFile(filePath,json) -> result ignored"],"errors":["The writeFile catch logs and resolves. The outer catch logs and resolves every failure.","DH rejection, ADS dialog 121, collection failure, or payload failure therefore skips the remaining work and resolves.","No per-ECU catch exists. The first collection rejection stops the sequential chain.","No unconditional communication/session cleanup exists. ADS cleanup occurs only in its explicit dialog branches."],"visible":["S701121","S701122","S70143 countdown","S701123","No normal report-send UI in this method"],"mutations":["mergeEquippedEcuList can mutate ecuGrpList","Read helpers mutate ECU/time/SWIN objects","Child swNoList arrays receive appended entries","JSON and report file","repro logs"],"cancellation":["Dialog responses are awaited without a clicked-value guard in the ADS branch. No cancel event is installed here."],"cleanup":["The ADS timer clears only when value > 10. Session and general communication end only in the two explicit ADS dialog branches."],"promise":"Returns a promise. Both the file-write catch and outer catch convert failure into successful resolution.","notes":[],"payload_shapes":{"envelope":{"sendVehicleInfo":{"SoftwareID":"commonInfo.getSoftwareId()","ID":"000000"},"reqData":{"vinNo":"vinNo argument","ecuInfo":[],"dcmLocalWriteTime":"","localWriteTime":"","ifHash":""}},"ecuData_initializer":"{ecuGrpId:ecuGrpId,ecuId:ecuId,busId:busId,phaseType:phaseType,validReadEcuPartNumberForPhase4:false,readEcuPartNumberForPhase4Data:[],validReadSubEcuPartNumber:false,readSubEcuPartNumberData:[],validReadEcuPartNumber:false,readEcuPartNumberData:[],validReadEcuPartNumberPhase6:false,readEcuPartNumberPhase6Data:[],isIncQuestionEcuPartNumberPhase6:false,validReadSoftwarePartNumber:false,readSoftwarePartNumberData:[],validReadSoftwarePartNumberPhase6:false,readSoftwarePartNumberPhase6Data:[],isIncQuestionSoftwarePartNumberPhase6:false,validReadEcuSerialNumber:false,readEcuSerialNumberData:[],isIncQuestionSerialNumberPhase6:false,readSubSerialNumberPhase6Data:[],validReadSubSerialNumberPhase6:false,isIncQuestionSubSerialNumberPhase6:false,validReadVehicleInformation:false,readVehicleInformationData:[],validGetCid:false,cidList:[],commConfig:undefined,ecuAssyNo:undefined,swNos:[],serialNo:undefined,subPartInfo:[],cBestData:'',swNoNum:0,isSuccessSendMessage8:false,isSuccessSendMessage9:false,isSuccessSendMessage52:false,isSuccessGetCid:false,isSurrogate:ecuInfo.isSurrogate}","parent":{"ecuAssyNo":"item.ecuAssyNo || empty string","hwPartNo":"item.ecuAssyNo || empty string","addressType":"","diagAddress":"","serialNo":"item.serialNo || empty string","swinList":[],"swNoList":[],"cBest":[{"cBestData":"item.cBestData"}]},"child":{"ecuAssyNo":"parent.ecuAssyNo || empty string","hwPartNo":"childInfo.hwPartNo || empty string","addressType":"parent.addressType || empty string","diagAddress":"parent.diagAddress || empty string","serialNo":"childInfo.serialNo || parent.serialNo || empty string","swinList":"parent.swinList reference","swNoList":"childInfo.swNoList reference","cBest":[{"cBestData":""}]}},"payload_rules":{"address_mapping":["Initialize addressType and diagAddress to empty strings. Require item.commConfig && item.commConfig.address before address mapping.","Address length 3 with truthy, nonempty nta: addressType=2, diagAddress=address+nta. Both addressType values are strings.","Address length 3 without truthy, nonempty nta: addressType=1, diagAddress=address.","Address length 4 with absent/falsy/empty nta: addressType=3, diagAddress=address.","Address length 2 with absent/falsy/empty nta: addressType=4, diagAddress=address.","Every other length/nta combination retains empty values. Surrogate addressType/diagAddress overrides the mapping."]}},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.sendVehicleInfoSwitchToAisac2","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-232-sendVehicleInfoSwitchToAisac2","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"sendVehicleInfoSwitchToAisac2","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-232-sendVehicleInfoSwitchToAisac2","prototype_index":232,"name":"sendVehicleInfoSwitchToAisac2","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[242853,243880],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["jsonFileName","oemDecisionInfoManual"],"state":["model.getSendVehicleJsonFolderPath","gts.FORMAT_DATA.SEND_VEHICLE_INFO"],"ordered_transitions":["Call getSendVehicleJsonFolderPath(oemDecisionInfoManual). Merge that folder and jsonFileName with gts.util.mergePath().","Read the file. Parse result.apiArgs.data as JSON.","Call checkHash(jsonData). For a truthy result, return replaceCtrlCharacter(jsonData,jsonFilePath). Otherwise reject {path:jsonFilePath,reason:ifHash is invalid.}.","Call adjustTimeField(json,true). Require gts.util.checkJsonFormat(json,gts.FORMAT_DATA.SEND_VEHICLE_INFO).","For a valid format, return doSendVehicleInfo(json,true,jsonFileName,oemDecisionInfoManual)."],"request_response":["model.getSendVehicleJsonFolderPath(oemDecisionInfoManual) -> folder string","model.readFile(jsonFilePath) -> {apiArgs:{data}}","model.checkHash(jsonData) -> truthy/falsy","model.replaceCtrlCharacter(jsonData,jsonFilePath) -> json","model.adjustTimeField(json,true) -> json","controller.doSendVehicleInfo(json,true,jsonFileName,oemDecisionInfoManual)"],"errors":["Invalid hash rejects {path:jsonFilePath,reason:ifHash is invalid.}. Invalid format rejects without a payload.","No local catch. Read, parse, transformation, and send failures propagate."],"visible":["No local view. doSendVehicleInfo owns send UI."],"mutations":["File-control-character replacement and time adjustment delegate to model helpers."],"cancellation":["No local cancel path."],"cleanup":["This method does not delete the JSON file."],"promise":"Returns the complete read/transform/send chain.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.writeVehicleInformationForA32","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-233-writeVehicleInformationForA32","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"writeVehicleInformationForA32","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-233-writeVehicleInformationForA32","prototype_index":233,"name":"writeVehicleInformationForA32","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[243880,250870],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["filePath","ecuGrpList","ts"],"state":["model.commonInfo","model.vin","surrogate ECU groups","ECU ID 8505 (IDS navigation)","phaseType 20 and 116"],"ordered_transitions":["Set utc=ts.substring(0,8) + T + ts.substring(8) + +0900. This constructs text without timezone conversion.","Set vinNo=model.vin.replace(/\\s+/g,empty string). Create the A32 envelope and naviInfo defaults in payload_shapes.","Call getCurretnVimFirmVersion(). Convert nullish version to empty string, remove every literal space, and truncate to 20 characters.","Store that value in headerInfo.vciHardwareVersion. Get surrogate groups and call mergeEquippedEcuList(ecuGrpList,surrogateEcuGrp).","Build one sequential promise chain across all group/ECU entries in iteration order.","For a surrogate ECU, synthesize connect=1. Otherwise call checkEcuConnect(ecuGrpId,ecuId,busId). Skip unless apiArgs.connect === 1.","The first connected ECU with ecuId === 8505 sets hasIds and naviInfo.ecuId/busId, then returns without a normal ECU read.","For every other connected ECU, create the exact ecuData initializer in payload_shapes. Copy surrogate addressType/diagAddress when applicable.","Append ecuData to ecuDataList. Append {ecuId,busId} to targetEcuList only for nonsurrogates. Return getEcuInfoA32(ecuData).","After collection, call getMileageInfo(targetEcuList). Store mileageInfo.value in headerInfo.odoMeter.","Call getVehicleModelName(). Store (modelName ?? empty string).replaceAll(literal space,empty string) in headerInfo.modelName.","If hasIds, call readNaviInfoA32(naviInfo). Otherwise skip the navigation read.","Filter records: phase 20 requires validReadEcuPartNumber && validReadSoftwarePartNumber && (isSuccessSendMessage8 || isSuccessSendMessage9).","Every other phase requires validGetCid && isSuccessGetCid. Get writtenCids=getCidListForWriteFlg().","For each phase-20 swNo, use procKey=item.procKeys[index]. Emit hwId=item.ecuAssyNo, swId=swNo, version=000 + procKey.charAt(9).","Initialize suDate, suResult, toolType to empty strings. If writtenCids.find(cid=>cid === procKey) is truthy, set suDate=utc,suResult=0,toolType=2. These last two values are strings.","If phase-20 item.swNos is empty, emit one record with hwId=item.ecuAssyNo and all other fields empty.","For phase 116, find CID_SUZUKI_HWID, CID_SUZUKI_SWID, CID_SUZUKI_SWVER in item.cidList. Use each found entry.data or empty string.","Use item.procKey ?? empty string for phase-116 write detection. Populate the same suDate, suResult, toolType values on a truthy written-CID match.","Other accepted phases emit no suResult record.","For each software result, clear hwId/swId when checkStringMatchPartId() fails. Clear version when checkStringMatchCommon() fails.","Remove a software result only when hwId,swId,version,suDate,suResult,toolType are all empty strings.","When hasIds, delete naviInfo.ecuId and busId. Validate hwId/swId with checkStringMatchPartId() and mapId with checkStringMatchCommon(), clearing failures.","Assign naviInfo as suResultInfoNavi. Without IDS, delete suResultInfoNavi.","Delete suResultInfo when its array is empty. Delete suResultInfoNavi when hwId,swId,version,mapId,mapVersion,suResult,suResultMap all have zero length.","Set updateVehicleInfo.ifHash=createHashA32(json). Call writeFile(filePath,json)."],"request_response":["model.getCurretnVimFirmVersion() -> firmVersion","model.checkEcuConnect(ecuGrpId,ecuId,busId) -> {apiArgs:{connect}}","model.getEcuInfoA32(ecuData) -> mutates ecuData","model.getMileageInfo(targetEcuList) -> {value}","model.getVehicleModelName() -> modelName","model.readNaviInfoA32(naviInfo) -> mutates naviInfo","model.getCidListForWriteFlg() -> writtenCids","model.createHashA32(json) -> hash","model.writeFile(filePath,json) -> result ignored"],"errors":["The file-write catch logs and resolves. The outer catch logs and resolves all earlier failures.","No per-ECU catch exists. A failure stops remaining collection and skips file creation.","Only the first connected IDS entry is special. Later entries with ecuId 8505 enter the normal collection branch."],"visible":["No local view or dialog."],"mutations":["ecuGrpList through mergeEquippedEcuList","ECU objects through model reads","naviInfo loses ecuId/busId","Report JSON and file"],"cancellation":["No local cancel path."],"cleanup":["No local communication cleanup."],"promise":"Returns the collection/write chain. All caught failures resolve successfully.","notes":[],"payload_shapes":{"envelope":{"terminalInfo":{"SoftwareID":"commonInfo.getSoftwareId()","ID":"000000"},"updateVehicleInfo":{"headerInfo":{"vehicleHealthDate":"ts","dealerName":"","applicationName":"GTS+","applicationVersion":"commonInfo.getApplicationPackageVersion()","vciSerialNo":"","vciHardwareVersion":"","modelName":"","vin":"model.vin with all whitespace removed","odoMeter":"","memo":""},"suResultInfo":"undefined initially","suResultInfoNavi":"undefined initially","ifHash":""}},"naviInfo":{"ecuId":"undefined","busId":"undefined","hwId":"","swId":"","version":"","mapId":"","mapVersion":"","suResult":"","suResultMap":""},"ecuData_initializer":"{ecuGrpId:ecuGrpId,ecuId:ecuId,busId:busId,phaseType:phaseType,validReadEcuPartNumber:false,readEcuPartNumberData:[],isSuccessSendMessage8:true,validReadSoftwarePartNumber:false,readSoftwarePartNumberData:[],isSuccessSendMessage9:true,validGetCid:false,isSuccessGetCid:false,cidList:[],ecuAssyNo:undefined,swNos:[],procKeys:[],isSurrogate:ecuInfo.isSurrogate}","software_result":{"hwId":"ECU-specific hardware ID","swId":"ECU-specific software ID","version":"ECU-specific version","suDate":"","suResult":"","toolType":""}}},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.sendVehicleInfoForA32","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-234-sendVehicleInfoForA32","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"sendVehicleInfoForA32","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-234-sendVehicleInfoForA32","prototype_index":234,"name":"sendVehicleInfoForA32","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[250870,253607],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":[],"state":["model.commonInfo.userInfo.loginMode","model.appName","commInfo.getWSSendVehicleInfoA32()","gts.FORMAT_DATA.SEND_VEHICLE_INFO_A32"],"ordered_transitions":["If loginMode === 2, resolve without sending. If model.appName is truthy, resolve without sending.","Read getWSSendVehicleInfoA32(). If sendVehicleInfo_url, getVehicleInfo_url, or id is falsy, log missing settings and resolve.","Get getSendVehicleJsonFolderPathA32(), then getSendVehicleFolderInfomation(jsonFolderPath).","Filter apiArgs.fileInfoList to exclude fileName starting with uppercase P. Sort ascending by new Date(lastUpdate).getTime().","The comparator returns -1 only when a time < b time. It returns 1 for equal, greater, or incomparable times.","Build a sequential chain for every retained file. Merge folder and filename, then call readFile(jsonFilePath).","JSON.parse(result.apiArgs.data). Require checkHashA32(jsonData). On success call replaceCtrlCharacterA32(jsonData,jsonFilePath).","Require checkJsonFormat(json,gts.FORMAT_DATA.SEND_VEHICLE_INFO_A32), then call doSendVehicleInfoA32(json,jsonFileName).","Only after a resolved send, call deleteFile(jsonFilePath).","Each file-chain catch logs the error and resolves. Continue with the next file."],"request_response":["commInfo.getWSSendVehicleInfoA32() -> {sendVehicleInfo_url,getVehicleInfo_url,id}","model.getSendVehicleJsonFolderPathA32() -> folder","model.getSendVehicleFolderInfomation(folder) -> {apiArgs:{fileInfoList:[{fileName,lastUpdate}]}}","model.readFile(path) -> {apiArgs:{data}}","model.checkHashA32(jsonData) -> truthy/falsy","model.replaceCtrlCharacterA32(jsonData,jsonFilePath) -> json","controller.doSendVehicleInfoA32(json,jsonFileName) -> resolved send or rejection","model.deleteFile(jsonFilePath) -> ignored result"],"errors":["Invalid hash rejects {path:jsonFilePath,reason:ifHash is invalid.}. Invalid format rejects without a payload.","Each file error is absorbed. Files are not deleted when a prior stage rejects.","Folder/list-chain errors log a file-information error and resolve."],"visible":["Only delegated doSendVehicleInfoA32 error dialogs."],"mutations":["File replacement delegates to the model","Successfully sent files are deleted"],"cancellation":["No local cancel path. A rejected send from user No is absorbed per file and does not stop later files."],"cleanup":["deleteFile runs only after send success."],"promise":"Returns Promise.resolve() for each skip guard. Otherwise returns the sequential file chain with caught failures.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.doSendVehicleInfoA32","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-235-doSendVehicleInfoA32","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"doSendVehicleInfoA32","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-235-doSendVehicleInfoA32","prototype_index":235,"name":"doSendVehicleInfoA32","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[253607,255231],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["jsonData","jsonFileName"],"state":["controller.viewAfterRecv","performance.now()"],"ordered_transitions":["Call model.sendVehicleInfoA32(jsonData). First require commonResult.statusCode === MIR2000000.","Then reject if commonResult.faultMessage is truthy.","Create a deferred and startTime=performance.now(). Schedule recursiveCheckResultOfSendInfoA32(controller,def,wsres.apiResult.ID,startTime,jsonFileName) after 1000 ms.","Return def.promise(). Any rejection enters the local catch.","If the rejection value is a function, use that function as showDialog. Otherwise define showDialog to call viewAfterRecv.showDialogS701107(jsonFileName).","The default dialog sets screenID to Screen: S701-107 after its promise resolves. The supplied function leaves screenID as empty string.","Call showDialog(). If clicked === Yes, append Yes repro log and recursively call this method with the same JSON and filename.","For every other choice, append No repro log and reject without payload."],"request_response":["model.sendVehicleInfoA32(jsonData) -> {commonResult:{statusCode,faultMessage},apiResult:{ID}}","viewAfterRecv.showDialogS701107(jsonFileName) -> {clicked}","Optional function-valued rejection -> dialog function returning a promise for {clicked}"],"errors":["Initial status/fault errors reject without a payload.","Submission and poll errors choose the retry dialog. A rejection thrown inside the catch handler propagates to the caller."],"visible":["Default S701107 filename retry dialog or supplied dialog function"],"mutations":["repro logs"],"cancellation":["Every choice other than Yes rejects. Yes retries without a retry-count limit."],"cleanup":["No local cleanup or file deletion."],"promise":"Returns the send/poll/retry chain. Each retry creates a fresh start time and deferred.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.recursiveCheckResultOfSendInfoA32","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-236-recursiveCheckResultOfSendInfoA32","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"recursiveCheckResultOfSendInfoA32","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-236-recursiveCheckResultOfSendInfoA32","prototype_index":236,"name":"recursiveCheckResultOfSendInfoA32","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[255231,256832],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["controller","def","id","startTime","jsonFileName"],"state":["performance.now()"],"ordered_transitions":["Call model.requestResultOfSendVehicleInfoA32(id).","For MIR2020000, reject def when elapsed time > 301000 ms. Otherwise schedule the same callback after 1000 ms.","For every other status, require MIR2000000. Reject def for a truthy commonResult.faultMessage.","Read wsres?.updateVehicleInfoResponse?.updateResultCode ?? 000. Require exact string 000.","Resolve def without a payload on success."],"request_response":["model.requestResultOfSendVehicleInfoA32(id) -> {commonResult:{statusCode,faultMessage},updateVehicleInfoResponse?:{updateResultCode?}}"],"errors":["Status, fault, non-000 updateResultCode, and timeout reject def without a payload.","The catch logs and rejects def without a payload. Timeout is checked only for MIR2020000.","jsonFileName is only carried to the next callback. This method does not use it in a request or dialog."],"visible":["No local UI."],"mutations":["Settles the caller-owned deferred"],"cancellation":["No cancellation guard."],"cleanup":["No stored timeout handle."],"promise":"Returns the request chain. The pending branch schedules another callback without returning def.promise().","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.checkVinAfterRepro","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-237-checkVinAfterRepro","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"checkVinAfterRepro","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-237-checkVinAfterRepro","prototype_index":237,"name":"checkVinAfterRepro","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[256832,258174],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":[],"state":["model.vin","controller.commonInfo.initVehicleConfirmation","CuwModel.DecisionVin"],"ordered_transitions":["If model.vin is falsy, return controller.releaseVim() without reading VINs.","Otherwise call processGetVINs(), retain its response, and then call controller.releaseVim().","Create allVins=[resGetVIN,dcm,airbag,ecgw,suzukiDcm]. Filter falsy values, then construct a Set to remove exact duplicates.","For one unique VIN equal to model.vin, resolve. For one unequal VIN, return showS701155(model.vin,uniqueVins[0]).","For zero VINs, inspect initVehicleConfirmation.decisionVin.","For MANUAL_NOT_CONFIRMED, MANUAL_CONFIRMED_BY_PID, or MANUAL_CONFIRMED_BY_MANUAL, showS70162AfterRepro(vehicleConfirmation.vinCode).","If its inputVin === model.vin, resolve. Otherwise showS701155(model.vin,inputVin).","For zero VINs with any other decision or no confirmation object, return showS701156().","For multiple unique VINs, return showS701155(model.vin,uniqueVins)."],"request_response":["model.processGetVINs() -> {resGetVIN,dcm,airbag,ecgw,suzukiDcm}","controller.releaseVim() -> ignored result","showS70162AfterRepro(initValue) -> inputVin","showS701155(beforeVin,connectedVin)","showS701156()"],"errors":["No local catch. Read, release, and view failures propagate.","The VIN list uses exact strings. It does not trim, uppercase, or otherwise normalize the received values.","releaseVim() follows a successful read. A processGetVINs rejection does not invoke releaseVim here."],"visible":["S701155 for mismatch/multiple VINs","S70162 for eligible manual confirmation","S701156 when VIN read has no result"],"mutations":["Only local VIN arrays and response reference"],"cancellation":["Retry and cancel behavior belongs to the selected view promise."],"cleanup":["releaseVim before comparing successful VIN reads, or immediately when model.vin is falsy. No finally cleanup."],"promise":"Returns the read/release/decision promise.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.showS701155","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-238-showS701155","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"showS701155","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-238-showS701155","prototype_index":238,"name":"showS701155","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[258174,259179],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["beforeVin","connectedVin (string or VIN array supplied by caller)"],"state":["controller.commonInfo","controller.viewReprogramCuw"],"ordered_transitions":["Create a deferred and ViewS701155.","On RETRY, log the operation and reject def with {isRetry:true}.","On CANCEL, log the operation and show S701121. After that dialog resolves, append its OK log and reject def without a payload.","Replace the view. Call viewS701155.init(beforeVin,connectedVin). After init resolves, return def.promise()."],"request_response":["viewS701155.init(beforeVin,connectedVin)","viewReprogramCuw.showDialogS701121() -> result ignored"],"errors":["The returned promise rejects for Retry, confirmed Cancel, or view init failure.","A S701121 rejection leaves the deferred unsettled because no local catch rejects it."],"visible":["ViewS701155 mismatch screen","S701121 after Cancel"],"mutations":["repro logs"],"cancellation":["CANCEL waits for S701121, then rejects. RETRY uses {isRetry:true}."],"cleanup":["Only delegated view replacement."],"promise":"Returns init().then(()=>def.promise()). It has no normal resolve path.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.showS701156","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-239-showS701156","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"showS701156","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-239-showS701156","prototype_index":239,"name":"showS701156","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[259179,260140],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":[],"state":["controller.commonInfo","controller.viewReprogramCuw"],"ordered_transitions":["Create a deferred and ViewS701156.","On RETRY, log the operation and reject def with {isRetry:true}.","On CANCEL, log the operation and show S701121. After that dialog resolves, append its OK log and reject def without a payload.","Replace the view. Call viewS701156.init(). After init resolves, return def.promise()."],"request_response":["viewS701156.init()","viewReprogramCuw.showDialogS701121() -> result ignored"],"errors":["The returned promise rejects for Retry, confirmed Cancel, or view init failure.","A S701121 rejection leaves the deferred unsettled because no local catch rejects it."],"visible":["ViewS701156 unavailable-VIN screen","S701121 after Cancel"],"mutations":["repro logs"],"cancellation":["CANCEL waits for S701121, then rejects. RETRY uses {isRetry:true}."],"cleanup":["Only delegated view replacement."],"promise":"Returns init().then(()=>def.promise()). It has no normal resolve path.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.showS70162AfterRepro","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-240-showS70162AfterRepro","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"showS70162AfterRepro","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-240-showS70162AfterRepro","prototype_index":240,"name":"showS70162AfterRepro","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[260140,260990],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["initValue"],"state":["model.inputVinCheck","CONFIG_KEY_INPUT_VIN_CHECK","controller.currentView"],"ordered_transitions":["Read CONFIG_KEY_INPUT_VIN_CHECK. Store inputVinCheckResult.value in model.inputVinCheck.","Create ViewS70162. On NEXT, read vin=evt.args[1], log S701-62 Next, and call checkVIN(controller,vin).","On successful validation, resolve def with the same vin. On validation rejection, restore currentView buttons and keep def unsettled.","Replace the view. Call viewS70162.init(initValue,true). After init resolves, return def.promise()."],"request_response":["model.getConfigParam(CONFIG_KEY_INPUT_VIN_CHECK) -> {value}","EVENT_BTN.NEXT evt.args[1] -> vin","controller.checkVIN(controller,vin)","viewS70162.init(initValue,true)"],"errors":["Configuration or init failure rejects the returned chain.","checkVIN rejection is absorbed after restoreBtn(). Another Next event can retry."],"visible":["ViewS70162 initialized for postwrite VIN entry"],"mutations":["model.inputVinCheck","repro log","Button restoration on failed validation"],"cancellation":["No cancel or back listener is installed in this method."],"cleanup":["Only delegated view replacement."],"promise":"Returns the configuration/init/deferred promise. Validation success resolves with vin.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.sendVinForSbr","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-241-sendVinForSbr","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"sendVinForSbr","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-241-sendVinForSbr","prototype_index":241,"name":"sendVinForSbr","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[260990,262457],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["ecuGrpList"],"state":["commonInfo.userInfo.loginMode","model.vin","controller.viewAfterRecv"],"ordered_transitions":["Evaluate vin=model.vin.trim() before the offline guard.","If loginMode === 2, return Promise.reject({code:offline}). This return occurs before the local catch chain.","Build {GTSTerminalInfo:{SoftwareID,SoftwareVersion},Request:{vin}} with the exact commonInfo getters.","Call doSendVinForSbr(json). Read sessionId=ssmResponse1?.ResponseData?.session_id without a presence check.","Create a deferred and record performance.now(). Schedule recursiveSendVinForSbr(controller,def,sessionId,startTime) after 1000 ms.","After polling resolves, return {session_id:sessionId,SSM5Response:ssmResponse2}.","On submission/poll-chain failure, call model.saveErrorReport(0), then viewAfterRecv.showDialogS701107(empty string).","If clicked === Yes, return controller.sendVehicleForSbr(ecuGrpList), not a direct VIN retry. Otherwise reject without payload."],"request_response":["controller.doSendVinForSbr({GTSTerminalInfo:{SoftwareID:commonInfo.getSoftwareId(),SoftwareVersion:commonInfo.getApplicationPackageVersion()},Request:{vin:model.vin.trim()}}) -> SSM5Response","model.saveErrorReport(0)","viewAfterRecv.showDialogS701107(empty string) -> {clicked}"],"errors":["Offline rejects {code:offline} without saving an error report or showing a local dialog.","A trim() error occurs before the returned chain. Error-report/dialog failures inside catch propagate.","On retry, sendVehicleForSbr may resolve undefined after absorbing its own failure. This method does not wrap that retry result as sessionInfo."],"visible":["S701107 on online submission/poll error"],"mutations":["Error report through model.saveErrorReport(0)"],"cancellation":["Dialog non-Yes rejects. Yes restarts the full SBR flow."],"cleanup":["No local cleanup or timer cancellation."],"promise":"Returns the initial/poll/sessionInfo chain, or the full-flow retry promise from its catch.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.doSendVinForSbr","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-242-doSendVinForSbr","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"doSendVinForSbr","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-242-doSendVinForSbr","prototype_index":242,"name":"doSendVinForSbr","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[262457,263093],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["json"],"state":["controller.model"],"ordered_transitions":["Call model.sendVinForSbr(json).","Require commonResult.statusCode === MIR2000000. Otherwise reject {statusCode:commonResult.statusCode}.","If commonResult.faultMessage is truthy, reject {faultMessage:commonResult.faultMessage}.","Read wsres.SSM5Response. Require ssmResponse?.ResponseData?.is_success === true.","If not true, reject {is_success:ssmResponse.ResponseData.is_success}. Otherwise resolve with ssmResponse."],"request_response":["model.sendVinForSbr(json) -> {commonResult:{statusCode,faultMessage},SSM5Response:{ResponseData:{is_success}}}"],"errors":["No local catch. Submission failures propagate.","The failed is_success branch dereferences ssmResponse.ResponseData without optional chaining. Missing objects can produce a TypeError instead of {is_success}."],"visible":["No local UI."],"mutations":["No controller state mutation."],"cancellation":["No local cancel path."],"cleanup":["No local cleanup."],"promise":"Returns a promise resolving to the entire SSM5Response object.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.recursiveSendVinForSbr","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-243-recursiveSendVinForSbr","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"recursiveSendVinForSbr","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-243-recursiveSendVinForSbr","prototype_index":243,"name":"recursiveSendVinForSbr","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[263093,264523],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["controller","def","sessionId","startTime"],"state":["controller.commonInfo","performance.now()"],"ordered_transitions":["Build {GTSTerminalInfo:{SoftwareID,SoftwareVersion},Request:{session_id:sessionId}}.","Call model.recursiveSendVinForSbr(json). Require MIR2000000, then reject a truthy faultMessage.","Read is_success=SSM5Response?.ResponseData?.is_success. Require is_success === true.","For process_status === processing, reject {reason:timeout} only when elapsed time > 900000 ms.","Otherwise schedule this callback after 5000 ms with unchanged session ID and start time. Return def.promise() in that processing branch.","For process_status === completed, resolve def with the entire SSM5Response.","For any other status, reject {process_status:procStatus,response:ssmResponse}."],"request_response":["model.recursiveSendVinForSbr({GTSTerminalInfo:{SoftwareID:commonInfo.getSoftwareId(),SoftwareVersion:commonInfo.getApplicationPackageVersion()},Request:{session_id:sessionId}}) -> {commonResult:{statusCode,faultMessage},SSM5Response:{ResponseData:{is_success,process_status}}}"],"errors":["Status failure rejects {statusCode}. Fault rejects {faultMessage}. A non-true success flag rejects {is_success}.","The catch rejects def with err, preserving request/callback error payloads.","The timeout applies only while process_status === processing. Completion can succeed after the time threshold."],"visible":["No local UI."],"mutations":["Settles the caller-owned deferred"],"cancellation":["No cancellation guard."],"cleanup":["No stored timeout handle or explicit cleanup."],"promise":"Returns the request chain. Processing adopts def.promise(), so that chain can remain pending across recursive timers.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.getEcuInfoForSbr","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-244-getEcuInfoForSbr","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"getEcuInfoForSbr","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-244-getEcuInfoForSbr","prototype_index":244,"name":"getEcuInfoForSbr","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[264523,267329],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["ecuGrpList","ssmResponse"],"state":["controller.commonInfo","CGW ecuId=722","CGW busId initially null","gts.ERROR_CODE.NO_RESPONSE"],"ordered_transitions":["Create the exact SBR envelope in payload_shapes. Initialize cgwBusId=null and ecuInfoList=[].","Build a sequential chain across every group/ECU entry. Capture ecuGrpId,ecuId,busId,ecuName,phaseType.","When iterating ecuId === 722, assign cgwBusId=busId before checking its connection. Later matches replace the earlier bus ID.","Call checkEcuConnect(ecuGrpId,ecuId,busId). Reject unless apiArgs.connect === 1.","Then call excuteSystemException(ecuId), then getEcuFunctionList(ecuId). Ignore their returned values.","On success append {ecuId,busId,phaseType,function_number:null,hw_id:null,sw_id:null,system_id:null,canId:null,ecuName} to the local collection.","Each ECU subchain catches every failure and resolves. Continue with later ECUs.","Start general communication with (722,cgwBusId). Set isGenCommStarted=true after that promise resolves.","Call readRxSwin(). Assign json.Request.rxswin=rxswin ?? [empty string]. Then call endGeneralComm().","On communication/read/end failure, call endGeneralComm() if communication started. After cleanup, rethrow only when err.errorCode === NO_RESPONSE. Absorb every other error.","Read systems=ssmResponse?.ResponseData?.systems ?? []. Build a second sequential chain for collected ECU objects.","For each object, call getEcuInfoSbr(ecuInfo). If ecuInfo.canId is truthy, find the first system with sys.canid === ecuInfo.canId.","Assign ecuInfo.function_number=target?.function_number. Then create {function_number,hw_id,sw_id,system_id}.","Append that system and the same ecuInfo object only when function_number !== null. Undefined passes this test.","After all reads, set json.cgwInfo={ecuId:722,busId:cgwBusId} and resolve json.","The outer catch resolves null for err.errorCode === NO_RESPONSE. It resolves the current, possibly partial json for other errors."],"request_response":["model.checkEcuConnect(ecuGrpId,ecuId,busId) -> {apiArgs:{connect}}","model.excuteSystemException(ecuId)","model.getEcuFunctionList(ecuId)","model.startGeneralComm(722,cgwBusId)","model.readRxSwin() -> rxswin","model.endGeneralComm()","model.getEcuInfoSbr(ecuInfo) -> mutates ECU object"],"errors":["The first loop absorbs per-ECU errors. The second loop has no per-ECU catch and stops on the first rejection.","A non-NO_RESPONSE error can return partial json before cgwInfo assignment.","Both error checks dereference err.errorCode directly. A null/undefined error can itself throw.","The inner cleanup can call endGeneralComm() again after an endGeneralComm rejection. A cleanup rejection propagates to the outer catch."],"visible":["No local UI."],"mutations":["Local ECU records through getEcuInfoSbr","json.Request.rxswin","json.Request.systems","json.ecuInfoList","json.cgwInfo"],"cancellation":["No local cancel path."],"cleanup":["Explicit general-communication cleanup surrounds only the CGW RXSWIN read. No finally surrounds the later ECU reads."],"promise":"Returns a promise resolving to a complete/partial JSON object or null for NO_RESPONSE, unless an error handler itself throws.","notes":[],"payload_shapes":{"initial":{"GTSTerminalInfo":{"SoftwareID":"commonInfo.getSoftwareId()","SoftwareVersion":"commonInfo.getApplicationPackageVersion()"},"Request":{"session_id":null,"rxswin":[""],"systems":[]},"ecuInfoList":[]},"system":{"function_number":"ecuInfo.function_number","hw_id":"ecuInfo.hw_id","sw_id":"ecuInfo.sw_id","system_id":"ecuInfo.system_id"},"added_after_success":{"cgwInfo":{"ecuId":722,"busId":"last encountered CGW busId, or null"}}}},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.updateRxSwin","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-245-updateRxSwin","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"updateRxSwin","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-245-updateRxSwin","prototype_index":245,"name":"updateRxSwin","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[267329,270146],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["cgwInfo:{ecuId,busId,rxswin}"],"state":["controller.viewAfterRecv","gts.ERROR_CODE.NO_RESPONSE","Local flags isGenCommStarted,isTransitSession,isSetNoResponseCondition start false"],"ordered_transitions":["Read ecuId,busId,rxswin from cgwInfo before constructing the returned chain.","For each rxswin string, require a space exists and its first occurrence is not the final character.","Encode every character as its charCodeAt(0). Require each code > 0x1F and < 0x7F.","Require each encoded string length <= 255. Append one length byte, then all ASCII bytes, to rxswinCode.","Require total rxswinCode length <= 1638. Append zero bytes until its length is exactly 1638.","Start general communication with (ecuId,busId), then set isGenCommStarted=true.","Call setNoResponseCondition(3,5000), then set isSetNoResponseCondition=true.","Call transitSession(3,false), then set isTransitSession=true.","Call requestSecurityAccessSbr(), then sendRxSwin(rxswinCode).","Call transitSession(1), then set isTransitSession=false.","Call removeNoResponseCondition() through a helper that absorbs its rejection. Then set isSetNoResponseCondition=false.","Call readRxSwin(). Store retrieved_rxswin=new_rxswin ?? [empty string]. Call endGeneralComm(). Resolve retrieved_rxswin.","On failure, first call transitSession(1) if isTransitSession. Then remove the no-response condition if its flag is set.","Then call endGeneralComm() if isGenCommStarted. After cleanup, if err.rxswin !== undefined && err.errorCode === NO_RESPONSE, reject without a payload.","Otherwise call saveErrorReport(0), then showDialogS701152(). For clicked === Yes, recursively retry updateRxSwin(cgwInfo). Every other choice resolves undefined."],"request_response":["model.startGeneralComm(cgwInfo.ecuId,cgwInfo.busId)","model.setNoResponseCondition(3,5000)","model.transitSession(3,false)","model.requestSecurityAccessSbr()","model.sendRxSwin(rxswinCode) -> exact 1638-byte numeric array","model.transitSession(1)","model.removeNoResponseCondition()","model.readRxSwin() -> RXSWIN array","model.endGeneralComm()","model.saveErrorReport(0)","viewAfterRecv.showDialogS701152() -> {clicked}"],"errors":["Validation rejects without payload. A failed validation enters catch with err undefined. The later direct err.rxswin access can throw before report/dialog.","Error cleanup is ordered. A session/end-communication cleanup rejection stops later cleanup and the report/dialog chain.","removeNoResponseCondition rejection is always absorbed by its helper, including during cleanup.","The special rxswin+NO_RESPONSE case rejects after cleanup and skips report/dialog.","No retry-count limit exists for Yes. Missing cgwInfo throws before the returned chain."],"visible":["S701152 after nonspecial errors when cleanup and error inspection succeed"],"mutations":["Local encoded buffer and cleanup flags","RXSWIN write through model.sendRxSwin","Error report through model.saveErrorReport(0)"],"cancellation":["Every S701152 choice other than Yes resolves undefined. There is no separate cancel listener."],"cleanup":["Success order: default session, remove no-response condition, read RXSWIN, end communication.","Failure order: default session if entered, remove condition if set, end communication if started.","isGenCommStarted remains true after endGeneralComm. The catch can attempt endGeneralComm again after a failed final end."],"promise":"Returns the encoding/write/read chain. A successful write returns the retrieved RXSWIN array. Declined retry returns undefined.","notes":["The first-space rule permits a leading space when that space is not the last character.","An empty rxswin array produces 1638 zero bytes and passes local encoding validation."]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.sendVehicleInfoForSbr","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-246-sendVehicleInfoForSbr","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"sendVehicleInfoForSbr","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-246-sendVehicleInfoForSbr","prototype_index":246,"name":"sendVehicleInfoForSbr","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[270146,272602],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["json","ecuGrpList"],"state":["controller.viewAfterRecv","json.Request.session_id","json.cgwInfo","json.ecuInfoList"],"ordered_transitions":["Capture sessionId, cgwInfo, and ecuInfoList from json. Delete json.cgwInfo and json.ecuInfoList before sending.","Call doSendVehicleInfoForSbr(json). Create a deferred and startTime=performance.now().","Schedule recursiveSendVehicleForSbr(controller,def,sessionId,startTime) after 1000 ms. Return def.promise().","If ssmResponse?.ResponseData?.needs_rxswin_update === true, set cgwInfo.rxswin=ssmResponse.ResponseData.rxswin.","Call updateRxSwin(cgwInfo). For a truthy rxswin result, set json.Request.rxswin=rxswin and recursively call sendVehicleInfoForSbr(json,ecuGrpList).","A falsy update result resolves without resending. A needs_rxswin_update value other than true also resolves.","On failure, read nonconformingList=err?.nonconforming ?? [] and is_invalid_configuration=err?.is_invalid_configuration ?? false.","Map each nonconforming sys.canid to the first captured ecuInfoList entry with matching canId. Append each found ecuName, preserving order and duplicates.","Call saveErrorReport(0). With nonconforming entries, create ViewS701150, replace the view, and call init(ecuNameList).","Otherwise, if is_invalid_configuration is truthy, showDialogS701151(). Otherwise showDialogS701107(empty string).","For clicked === Yes, restart sendVehicleForSbr(ecuGrpList). For clicked === OK, reject {is_invalid_configuration}.","For clicked === lowercase next, reject {nonconforming:nonconformingList,ecuNameList}. Every other choice rejects {reason:S701-107 No button}."],"request_response":["controller.doSendVehicleInfoForSbr(json) -> SSM5Response","controller.updateRxSwin(cgwInfo) -> RXSWIN array or undefined","model.saveErrorReport(0)","ViewS701150.init(ecuNameList) -> {clicked}","viewAfterRecv.showDialogS701151() -> {clicked}","viewAfterRecv.showDialogS701107(empty string) -> {clicked}"],"errors":["No outer catch surrounds the error handler. Report, view, mapping, and retry failures can propagate.","The recursive RXSWIN resend receives the same JSON after cgwInfo and ecuInfoList deletion. Its new local captures are undefined.","On that recursive call, another requested RXSWIN update cannot assign cgwInfo.rxswin. A nonconforming mapping cannot call ecuInfoList.find().","The code does not restore deleted metadata before the recursive resend."],"visible":["ViewS701150 with nonconforming ECU names","S701151 for invalid configuration","S701107 for other errors"],"mutations":["Deletes json.cgwInfo and json.ecuInfoList","cgwInfo.rxswin assignment","json.Request.rxswin after successful update","Error report"],"cancellation":["Yes restarts the full flow. OK, next, and every other choice return distinct rejection payloads."],"cleanup":["View replacement only for S701150. No local communication cleanup or timeout cancellation."],"promise":"Returns the submit/poll/update/resend chain. Its catch returns retry or an explicit rejection.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.doSendVehicleInfoForSbr","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-247-doSendVehicleInfoForSbr","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"doSendVehicleInfoForSbr","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-247-doSendVehicleInfoForSbr","prototype_index":247,"name":"doSendVehicleInfoForSbr","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[272602,273255],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["json"],"state":["controller.model"],"ordered_transitions":["Call model.sendVehicleInfoForSbr(json). Require commonResult.statusCode === MIR2000000.","Reject {statusCode} on a different code. Reject {faultMessage} for a truthy fault message.","Read ssmResponse=wsres?.SSM5Response. Require ssmResponse?.ResponseData?.is_success === true.","If not true, reject {is_success:ssmResponse.ResponseData.is_success}. Otherwise resolve ssmResponse."],"request_response":["model.sendVehicleInfoForSbr(json) -> {commonResult:{statusCode,faultMessage},SSM5Response:{ResponseData:{is_success}}}"],"errors":["No local catch. Model/request errors propagate.","A missing SSM5Response or ResponseData can throw on the failed-success branch because the rejection payload dereferences both directly."],"visible":["No local UI."],"mutations":["No controller state mutation."],"cancellation":["No local cancel path."],"cleanup":["No local cleanup."],"promise":"Returns the model request chain, resolving to the complete SSM5Response.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
  {"id":"FlashingFrontend.controller.recursiveSendVehicleForSbr","original_contract_id":"cuw-controller-248-recursiveSendVehicleForSbr","unit_id":"flashing.ui.js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","method":"recursiveSendVehicleForSbr","semantic_contract":{"id":"cuw-controller-248-recursiveSendVehicleForSbr","prototype_index":248,"name":"recursiveSendVehicleForSbr","source":{"member":"js/cuw/controllers/cuw_controller.js","sha256":"a620b310a4bd2ff8e2733dce1e4030b7f6380e7464a4aceb89038010f765ebc5","char_span":[273255,275107],"char_span_convention":"zero-based half-open Unicode characters after UTF-8 BOM removal"},"inputs":["controller","def","sessionId","startTime"],"state":["controller.commonInfo","performance.now()"],"ordered_transitions":["Build {GTSTerminalInfo:{SoftwareID,SoftwareVersion},Request:{session_id:sessionId}}.","Call model.recursiveSendVehicleForSbr(json). Require MIR2000000, then reject a truthy faultMessage.","Require SSM5Response?.ResponseData?.is_success === true. Otherwise reject {is_success}.","For process_status === processing, reject {reason:timeout} only when elapsed time > 900000 ms.","Otherwise schedule this callback after 5000 ms with unchanged arguments. Return def.promise() in that branch.","For process_status === completed, read systems=ResponseData.systems ?? []. Select every system with is_nonconforming === true.","If that list is nonempty, reject {nonconforming:nonconformingList} before inspecting invalid configuration.","Otherwise, if ResponseData.is_invalid_configuration === true, reject {is_invalid_configuration:true}.","Otherwise resolve def with the complete SSM5Response.","For every other process_status, reject {process_status:procStatus,response:ssmResponse}."],"request_response":["model.recursiveSendVehicleForSbr({GTSTerminalInfo:{SoftwareID:commonInfo.getSoftwareId(),SoftwareVersion:commonInfo.getApplicationPackageVersion()},Request:{session_id:sessionId}}) -> {commonResult:{statusCode,faultMessage},SSM5Response:{ResponseData:{is_success,process_status,systems?,is_invalid_configuration?}}}"],"errors":["Direct status/fault checks reject {statusCode} or {faultMessage}. Direct non-true success rejects {is_success}.","The catch always calls def.reject() without err. Request/callback rejection details are discarded.","In the processing branch, returning def.promise() also lets this catch run when a later poll rejects that deferred.","Timeout is checked only for processing. A completed response can succeed after the threshold."],"visible":["No local UI."],"mutations":["Settles the caller-owned deferred"],"cancellation":["No cancellation guard."],"cleanup":["No stored timeout handle."],"promise":"Returns the request chain. Processing adopts def.promise(), so the chain can remain pending across recursive timers.","notes":[]},"contract_fragment":"oemsecurity","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.cuw-controller"]},
