  {"id":"upgrade.worker.initUpgrade","inputs":{"model":"bound worker instance","param":"unused"},"outputs":"Promise<void>","ordered_semantics":["Replace initData with source-defined folder/file/VIN/software/request/response/ECU maps and lists; initial cuwMaxNum=16.","Replace downloadData with URL/download list/request/serviceUrl state and downloadCalFileNum=0."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["Does not reset isCancel; getVin does reset it. Full initializer shape is retained in source adjunct."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.getEquippedEcuList","inputs":{"model":"bound instance","param":"unused"},"outputs":"Promise<{isComError:boolean}>","ordered_semantics":["Initialize isComError=false; local getEquippedEcuListFunc is an already-resolved promise and sends no PF request.","Clear initData.ecuInfoList; enumerate mountedEcuMap values in Object.keys order.","For PHASE_5(20) or isPhaseType6(PHASE_6=22), append serial promise stages: await ecuInfo.getEcuStatus({checkDisconnected:true}), then append ecuInfo regardless returned status.","Resolve {isComError:false}."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["No catch in this method: rejection from getEcuStatus (e.g. system-exception replacement) propagates."],"edge_cases":["Other OEM phase constants are excluded here, including MAZDA_OEM21/SUBARU_OEM52/DAIHATSU_UDS84/SUZUKI_P5=116; no entitlement or supply branch inferred."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.getVin","inputs":{"model":"bound instance","param":"unused"},"outputs":"Promise<{isShowDl005:boolean}>","ordered_semantics":["Reset isCommunicating/isSessionMode3/isCancel=false; call PF getVin({}), trim through API wrapper then padEnd(17,\" \"). On truthy result append VIN labeled by engine ECU372, else EV_FC397, else empty system name.","Sequentially visit DCM459 (fixed bus34), first existing DCM phase6 ECU in [6064,6564] (its bus), SRS_AIRBAG444 (fixed bus18), first existing phase6 airbag ECU in [6025,6525] (its bus). Skip each absent ECU.","For each present target: startGeneralComm({ecuId,busId}) => flag communicating=true; transitSession({modeId:1}) => session3=false; transitSession({modeId:3}) => session3=true; SendMessageForUtility({reqType:0,reqBody:[0x22,0xF1,0x90]}) for DCM or [0x22,0x10,0x15] for airbag.","Send helper strips reqBody.length bytes from response.apiArgs.resBody; failed send resolves undefined. checkReadVIN accepts only nonempty bytes whose first byte is not 0x00/0x3f/0xff; accepted bytes pass convertAscii; truthy VIN appends {system:ecuName,vin} without 17-character padding.","After each target attempt cleanup, then next target. Resolve isShowDl005 = (vinList.length===0)."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Initial getVin failure/padding failure resolves undefined; each target communication chain catches and resolves before afterProcess.","afterProcess: if session3 flag, try mode1 then endGeneralComm; failure of mode1/end leads another endGeneralComm. Else if communicating flag, endGeneralComm. end errors swallowed; only successful end clears communicating flag and only successful mode1 clears session3 flag.","Outer catch invokes onErrorCommon, rejecting without original error. isCancel is not consulted in any VIN step."],"edge_cases":["vinList is appended, not cleared; initUpgrade must establish it."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.checkVinMatch","inputs":{"param.parameter.vin":"optional string"},"outputs":"Promise<{isShowDl006:boolean,vinList:Array<{system,vin}>}>","ordered_semantics":["If supplied VIN truthy, append padded-to-at-least17 entry with engine372/EV397 label or empty string.","Compare each stored VIN against vinList[0].vin using strict string inequality; any mismatch sets isShowDl006.","If no mismatch, set initData.vin=vinList[0].vin; resolve all entries and mismatch flag."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["Empty vinList throws synchronously on vinList[0].vin when no mismatches; mismatching list leaves prior initData.vin unchanged. Padding never truncates or normalizes case."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.getEachInformationPhase5","inputs":{"initData.ecuInfoList":"ordered candidates"},"outputs":"Promise<{isShowDl003:boolean}>","ordered_semantics":["Reset communication flags, ecuDataMap={}, isSkip=false, isShowDl003=false; iterate ECU list through serial promise chain and collect only successfully configured ECUs.","For each PHASE6 ECU checkEcuConnect with current mounted {groupId,ecuId,busId}; only connect===1 continues. PHASE5 follows same connectivity rule but excludes ECU IDs374,399,457. Other phase types skip.","Initialize ecuData={ecuId,ecuAssyNo:undefined,writeFlg:0,cidList:[],rob:undefined,commConfig:undefined}; start communication, mode1, mode3.","PHASE6 read [22,F1,91]: if returned data truthy, maxByte=data[1], convertAscii(data,3,maxByte,true) into ecuAssyNo. Read [22,F1,88]: partNum=data[0], length=data[1], pos=2; per part increment pos once, parse12 bytes with phase6 validation, keep truthy CID unless indexOf(\"#\",10)===10, then advance pos by length.","PHASE5 read [22,01,05], convertAscii(data,0,12) into assy number. Read [22,F1,81]: part count first byte then fixed16 bytes each. Any CID containing ! sets writeFlg1 and Dl003; truthy CIDs append.","Each communication-chain failure sets isSkip=true, then cleanup afterProcess. Send helper failures themselves resolve undefined, so absent read data alone does not set isSkip.","If not skipped: PHASE6 getEcuFuncList must contain function48 whose detail list has id1 before getRob({ecuId,funcDivId:2,getRobStatus:2,userDefDtcList:[{funcId:48,funcDetailIdList:[{funcDetailId:1}]}]}). PHASE5 always getRob({ecuId,funcDivId:2,getRobStatus:2}).","Assign returned ROB; PHASE6 sets writeFlg1/Dl003 when behaviorCodeList element dispCode XU230351 or XU230451 and kind includes numeric1. PHASE5 sets same if rawCode numeric0xf021 or0xf022.","If not skipped getCommConfig({ecuId,busId}); only truthy returned apiArgs stores ecuData in map and appends ECU. Replace ecuInfoList with successful connected/configured list; resolve Dl003."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["checkEcuConnect/getRob/getCommConfig catches return undefined. PHASE6 ROB error calls outputLog (no-op). Cleanup matches getVin and swallows end errors.","No final catch; unexpected errors outside guarded subchains propagate. No isCancel checks."],"edge_cases":[],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.writeSendingData","inputs":{"initData":"VIN and ECU metadata"},"outputs":"Promise<{}>","ordered_semantics":["PF getSpecificFolder({folderNo:2}); use folderInfoList[0].folderInfo as specificFolderPath. PF getSettingFileInfo({fileType:2,keyList:[\"specificSubFolders\",\"softwareasaPartJSONFile\"]}); merge folder/fileData to jsonFilePath. PF getSoftwareId({}); store softwareId.","Create S_<vin>_<local YYYYMMDDhhmmss>.json and sendingData={sendSearchInfo:{SoftwareID:softwareId,ID:\"000000\"},reqData:{vinNo:vin,ecuInfo:[],upgradeFlg:\"0\"}}.","For each retained ECU get ecuDataMap metadata. diagAddress=commConfig.address, addressType defaults3; address length3 with truthy nta => addressType2 and concatenate nta, length3 without nta =>1, length2 =>4.","Append {ecuId:String(ecuId),ecuAssyNo:assy??\"\",diagAddress,addressType:String(type),writeFlg:numeric,swNoList:cidList.length?cidList.map(cid=>({swNo:cid??\"\"})):[{swNo:\"\"}]}. Store sendingData.","PF writeFile({path:mergePath(jsonFilePath,sendSearchInfoFileName),mode:0,data:JSON.stringify(sendingData)}), then resolve {}."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Folder/setting/software/write failures swallowed individually; they do not abort later steps. Outer onErrorCommon discards unexpected error reason."],"edge_cases":[],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.sendCancel","inputs":{},"outputs":"Promise<void>","ordered_semantics":["Set model.isCancel=true; resolve."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["Flag only; no PF cancel request, abort signal, timer cancellation, or reset."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.sendSearchSwAsc2","inputs":{"commonInfo.settingFileInfo.distributorDepending.countryInformation.userType.filePath":"setting file path"},"outputs":"Promise<{isCancel:boolean,isShowDl007:boolean}>","ordered_semantics":["PF getSettingFileInfo({filePath:userType.filePath,keyList:[\"softwareAsaPartSearchInfoAisac2\"]}); parse response.apiArgs.fileData with SettingType.OBJECT into initData.urlInfo.","If isCancel skip web request; otherwise POST JSON.stringify(sendingData) to urlInfo.sendSearchInfo_url with serverId=urlInfo.id.","Parse response.apiArgs.responseData JSON; accept only commonResult.statusCode===\"MIR2000000\" and falsy faultMessage. Compute SHA-256 of apiResult.ID as TEXT, uppercase HEX; store receiveDataRequestParam={requestSearchInfo:{ID,HashValue}}. Otherwise Dl007=true.","Resolve current isCancel and Dl007."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Settings error sets Dl007 but does not guard the web stage; web-stage errors/JSON errors/hash errors set Dl007. Outer onErrorCommon drops unexpected reason.","Cancel is checked only before dispatch; in-flight response still mutates request state."],"edge_cases":[],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.receiveSearchSwAsc2","inputs":{"initData.urlInfo/receiveDataRequestParam":"search polling metadata"},"outputs":"Promise<{isCancel,isShowDl004,isShowDl007,isShowDl017,time}>","ordered_semantics":["If isCancel or local Dl007, skip polling. Else define POST to urlInfo.requestSearchInfo_url with requestData=JSON.stringify(receiveDataRequestParam), serverId=urlInfo.id.","Always wait first1000ms using deferred/setTimeout; increment timeCount only on waits; mark timeout at >=300000ms. Each attempt checks isCancel before request.","MIR2000000 with falsy faultMessage stores entire response in saveRequestSearchInfo and apiResult in receivingData, even after timeout. MIR2000000 with fault sets Dl007. MIR2020000 waits/recurses only while !isTimeout; all other codes Dl007.","After polling, if !Dl007 call writeRequestSearchInfo even when cancellation skipped polling; no cancel guard around write.","Inspect receivingData?.responseMessageList||[] for ME10012 => Dl017=true, format receivingData.plannedOutageTime. Inspect resData.ecuInfo -> rootInfo -> swVerInfo for suType===\"1\" => Dl004. Resolve flags/current isCancel/time."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Each web/parse failure sets Dl007; outer onErrorCommon drops unexpected reason. Cancellation does not clear pending timeout/in-flight request or prior receivingData."],"edge_cases":["Timeout measures accumulated deliberate waits, not wall time spent servicing requests."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.sendSearchSwAsc2Upgrade","inputs":{},"outputs":"Promise<{isCancel,isShowDl007}>","ordered_semantics":["Mutate sendingData.reqData.upgradeFlg=\"1\" and regenerate S_<vin>_<local timestamp>.json filename.","Write sendingData JSON mode0 before any cancel check.","Then same sendSearchInfo_url POST, MIR2000000/falsy fault check, uppercase SHA256 ID requestSearchInfo ticket construction as initial sendSearchSwAsc2.","Return current cancel and Dl007."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Write failure swallowed. Dispatch guarded by isCancel; in-flight mutation not canceled. Web/parse/hash errors set Dl007; outer onErrorCommon loses reason."],"edge_cases":["upgradeFlg here requests ECU software upgrade search; no GTS application-version/update operation."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.receiveSearchSwAsc2Upgrade","inputs":{},"outputs":"Promise<{isShowDl007:boolean}>","ordered_semantics":["Same 1-second initial wait and MIR2020000 5-minute accumulated-wait search polling as receiveSearchSwAsc2; accept MIR2000000/falsy fault even if timeout already true.","Cancel checked at entry and before each request; successful response updates saveRequestSearchInfo and receivingData.","If !Dl007 writeRequestSearchInfo regardless cancellation, then return Dl007 only."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Web/parse errors set Dl007, outer onErrorCommon rejects without reason."],"edge_cases":["Does not return isCancel/Dl004/Dl017/time; those distinctions belong later screen judgment."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.judgeNextScreen","inputs":{"initData.receivingData":"API result","initData.sendingData":"request snapshot","commonInfo.userInfo.language.code":"label locale"},"outputs":"Promise<screen-branch union>","ordered_semantics":["Look for responseMessageList[].responseMessage===\"ME10012\"; if present return {isCancel,isShowDl017:true,time:makeLocaleTime(plannedOutageTime)} immediately.","If no truthy ecuId in receivingData?.resData?.ecuInfo||[], return {isCancel,isShowDl008:true}.","If any syncReproInfo[].syncReproTargetInfo[].diagAddress truthy: for every received ECU find FIRST sync group containing equal diagAddress via nested some, then require every target in that group to have an exact diagAddress match in sendingData.reqData.ecuInfo. A received ECU with no matching group gets empty targetList and passes. Failure returns {isCancel,isShowDl010:true}.","PF setting {fileType:1,keyList:[\"softwareAsaPartCuwMaxNum\"]}; parse NUMBER, nullish fallback16; failure fallback16. Then setting {fileType:2,keyList:[\"specificSubFolders\",\"softwareasaPartCALFile\"]}; merge to calFilePath.","createUpdateList step2Map groups request ECU IDs and concatenates all truthy swNo values, preserving duplicates/order.","Iterate response ecuInfo/rootInfo/swVerInfo/swInfo in nested source order. Skip ECU if no step2Map entry. Keep candidate only if EVERY sent swNo does not start with candidate swInfo.swNo (sendSwNo.indexOf(swInfo.swNo)!==0). Create row with response ECU/version/software fields, local suName (ja=>suNameJp else suNameEn), status0/isSelected=false, all four original indices, syncReproInfoIndex undefined; append and index by four-index key in duplexCheckMap and ECU ID in step4Map.","For each initial candidate and EVERY sync group: build targetList of all targets not matching candidate swVariation/version/diagAddress; if at least one exact triple matched, retain {info,targetList,syncReproInfoIndex} in step6Map for candidate ECU. The outer sync-group loop does not break on a matched group.","For each retained sync target iterate response ECU by equal diagAddress, version by exact version/swVariation, then swInfo. Again require EVERY sent swNo for that ECU not prefixed by candidate swNo. Existing four-index row only gets syncReproInfoIndex assigned if currently nullish; absent row gets same full row fields and this group index, then append. First candidate itself is not automatically tagged unless reached as a target.","If updateList empty Dl008=true/S001=false, otherwise Dl008=false/S001=true. Build cidListMap directly from ecuDataMap entries. Return {isCancel,isShowDl008,isShowS001,cuwMaxNum,selectedNum:0,updateList,cidListMap,calFilePath}."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["CAL setting failure swallowed and leaves prior path; unexpected shape/missing step2Map access or malformed outage time goes to onErrorCommon. No cancellation guard beyond returning isCancel; no actual launch or selection limit enforcement here."],"edge_cases":["Rows retain latestFlg,restoreFlg,distOperationFlg,canOTAFlg,canBlankEcuReproFlg,suNo,suName,suType,swVariation,version,swNo,comment,filePath,fileName,hash,fileSize,fileEntityFlg,reproOrder,ecuAssyNo,diagAddress,addressType,ecuId and original four indices. Hash is metadata here, not verified.","Address matching and all flags use exact source comparisons; this method adds no OEM-specific branch or application-update logic."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.checkLocalStorage","inputs":{"param.parameter.selectedRowList":"array of selected rows containing swNoList"},"outputs":"Promise<{isShowS005,isShowS006,isShowDl011,dl011ViewData,downloadCalFileNum}>","ordered_semantics":["Store selectedRowList by reference. PF list calFilePath with *.cuw/*.CUW/*.scuw/*.SCUW/*.cuwd/*.CUWD; default fileInfoList[] and deduplicate exact fileName via exceptDuplexFileInfoList.","Call synchronous checkFindCalFile; serially delete every returned deleteCalFileList name under calFilePath, swallowing each failure.","If isExecuteRepro set S006=true; else call synchronous checkSelectedFileSize. If a size result exists and Dl011 false, set S005=true.","Return S005/S006, optional checkFileSizeResult?.isShowDl011 and ?.dl011ViewData (undefined when all files local), plus current downloadCalFileNum."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["List failure swallowed, retaining prior calFileInfoList. Unexpected failures go to onErrorCommon. No isCancel check."],"edge_cases":["Deletes happen before aggregate size check. isShowDl011 return uses optional result, not local initialized false."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.checkFindCalFile","inputs":{"initData.selectedRowList":"rows with swNoList","calFileInfoList":"local file entries","receivingData.resData.ecuInfo":"search result autonomous metadata"},"outputs":"{deleteCalFileList:Array<string>,isExecuteRepro:boolean,downloadFileNum:0}","ordered_semantics":["Reset clearRobEcuIdMap={}, downloadList=[], downloadCalFileNum=0. Build case-folded local filename map; initialize return isExecuteRepro=true and downloadFileNum=0.","For each selected software entry in row/order: resolve ECU phase from Number(elm.ecuId). ZIP branch is uppercased fileName matching /ZIP$/ (no dot requirement), deduplicated globally by uppercase ZIP filename.","ZIP branch: scan every receiving ECU autonomousInfo[].improvementInfo[]; count entries whose uppercased fileName equals selected ZIP. Per match, if phase5 and Number(restoreFlg)===1, record ecuId in clearRob map. Count every local calibration filename containing elm.swNo case-insensitively; collect those names.","ZIP is considered complete iff local count>0 AND equal to search match count. Otherwise isExecuteRepro=false, concatenate all matching local names for deletion, enqueue selected ZIP once, add search match count to downloadCalFileNum.","Non-ZIP branch: if exact case-insensitive filename present, phase5 restore1 records clearRob ECU; otherwise set isExecuteRepro=false, enqueue entry, increment downloadCalFileNum1.","Return working result; returned downloadFileNum is never incremented."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["No byte length/hash verification, count only. ZIP clearRob map may be set even if local files incomplete; ordinary missing file does not set map until later checkReproFile reruns. autonomousInfo/improvementInfo missing causes synchronous error."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.checkSelectedFileSize","inputs":{"selectedRowList":"rows with swNoList fileName/fileSize"},"outputs":"{isShowDl011:boolean,dl011ViewData?:{limitFileSize:number,sumFileSize:number,fileList:Array}}","ordered_semantics":["Empty rows return false. For ALL selected entries with truthy fileName (not only downloads), fileSize truthy => parseInt(base10), else default300*1024*1024. Sum raw bytes; display each ceil(bytes/MiB)+\"MB\".","If sum<=10240*1024*1024 return false. Otherwise return true with limitFileSize10240, ceil(sum/MiB), and per-file list."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["No duplicate suppression or invalid-size validation; NaN makes <= comparison false and propagates into displayed sum."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.makeListFile","inputs":{"param.parameter.swNoList":"array of {swNo,fileName}"},"outputs":"Promise<{path:string|undefined,name:string}>","ordered_semantics":["Generate L_<vin>_<local YYYYMMDDhhmmss>.txt in calFilePath.","For each software entry append 1-based ordinal + comma + swNo + comma + fileName + CRLF. No CSV escaping/quoting.","PF writeFile({path:mergePath(outputData.path,name),mode:0,data:assembledText}); resolve folder path and filename."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Write failure swallowed; outer onErrorCommon drops unexpected error reason."],"edge_cases":[],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.sendDownloadCalFile","inputs":{"downloadData.downloadList":"missing software entries","softwareId":"stored ID","userType.filePath":"settings path"},"outputs":"Promise<{isShowDl007,isSkipRcvDlCalFile}>","ordered_semantics":["PF getSettingFileInfo({filePath:userType.filePath,keyList:[\"softwareAsaPartDownloadtoCalFileAisac2\"]}); parse object into calFileUrl; failure swallowed.","If no calFileUrl => Dl007. Else POST to calFileUrl.downloadtoCalFile_url with serverId=id and JSON {downloadtoCalFile:{SoftwareID:softwareId,ID:\"000000\"},reqData:downloadList.map(elm=>({swNo,fileName,filePath}))}.","Only MIR2000000 plus falsy faultMessage accepted; if apiResult.URL truthy, store serviceUrl and isSkipRcvDlCalFile=true. Else build receiveDataRequestParam={requestDownloadtoCalFileURL:{ID:apiResult.ID,HashValue:uppercaseSHA256TEXT(ID)}}.","Return Dl007 and skip-poll flag."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Web/JSON/hash errors => Dl007; outer onErrorCommon drops reason. No cancel checks."],"edge_cases":["Failed setting lookup can leave stale prior calFileUrl; only falsiness is checked."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.receiveDownloadCalFile","inputs":{"downloadData.calFileUrl/receiveDataRequestParam":"download URL ticket"},"outputs":"Promise<{isShowDl007}>","ordered_semantics":["POST JSON request ticket to calFileUrl.requestDownloadtoCalFileURL_url with serverId=id. Wait1000ms before first attempt; increment timeout counter only on timer waits; timeout at900000ms.","MIR2000000 with faultMessage OR timeout => Dl007; otherwise truthy apiResult.URL => store serviceUrl and finish; success without URL waits and recurses.","MIR2020000 while !timeout waits and recurses; any other code => Dl007. Return flag."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Web/JSON errors => Dl007, outer onErrorCommon drops reason. No cancellation checks, no timer cancellation."],"edge_cases":["Unlike search polling, successful URL at timeout is rejected. 15-minute bound excludes request durations."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.downloadtocalFile","inputs":{"downloadData.serviceUrl":"remote binary URL","calFilePath":"local destination"},"outputs":"Promise<{isShowDl007}>","ordered_semantics":["Generate local YYYYMMDDhhmmss.zip. PF downloadFile({url:serviceUrl,folderPath:mergePath(calFilePath,filename),authHeader:true}). Failure sets Dl007 and skips all extraction.","List ALL *.zip in calFilePath, not just downloaded filename. On nonempty list select first entry, run extractFunc, then recursively re-list until no entries.","extractFunc: PF extractFile({fromPath:calFilePath/zip,toPath:calFilePath/tmp}); list tmp matching cuw/CUW/zip/ZIP/scuw/SCUW/cuwd/CUWD; exact-case dedupe filenames.","Serially move each extracted listed entry from tmp/name to calFilePath with overwrite:true. Then delete tmp path, then delete original ZIP. Nested ZIP moved to parent becomes a later recursive extraction candidate.","Return Dl007, which represents download failure only."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Each extraction/list/move/delete error is swallowed; listings fail to empty array. Unexpected errors outer onErrorCommon. No cancellation checks or hash verification.","Failed ZIP deletion with recurring successful listing may cause indefinite recursive attempts; no count/timeout guard in source. All existing *.zip are subject to processing."],"edge_cases":[],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.checkReproFile","inputs":{},"outputs":"Promise<{fileList:Array<{fileName:string}>}>","ordered_semantics":["Re-list calFilePath with cuw/CUW/scuw/SCUW/cuwd/CUWD and dedupe exact names.","Rerun checkFindCalFile (resetting clearRob/download lists and count); if isExecuteRepro false return each remaining downloadList entry as {fileName}; else empty fileList."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["List failure swallowed and leaves stale calFileInfoList; unexpected error onErrorCommon."],"edge_cases":["Does not itself delete files returned by checkFindCalFile or launch reprogramming."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.checkCuwConnect","inputs":{},"outputs":"Promise<number|undefined>","ordered_semantics":["PF checkConnectionNameExist({name:\"CUW\"}); read apiArgs.existNum, catch to undefined.","Only when existNum===numeric0: flatten selectedRowList[].swNoList[] to mergePath(calFilePath,fileName) strings preserving order/duplicates; write JSON array to mergePath(calFilePath,\"cuwFileList.json\") with mode1.","Return existNum unchanged, whether write succeeds or fails; for any other value (including undefined) skip file write."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Check failure returns undefined; write failure swallowed; outer onErrorCommon drops reason."],"edge_cases":["No window launch, native process launch, port construction, vehicle programming, or implicit clearing occurs here. Controller-owned launch follows this preparation seam."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.clearRob","inputs":{"clearRobEcuIdMap":"map from local checks"},"outputs":"Promise<void>","ordered_semantics":["Enumerate Object.keys(clearRobEcuIdMap), serially call PF clearRob({ecuId:Number(key)}).","Swallow every per-call and per-stage failure, then resolve void."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["No cancel guard and no map clearing. Outer onErrorCommon for unexpected failure."],"edge_cases":[],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.mergePath","inputs":{"parentPath":"optional string","childPath":"optional string"},"outputs":"string|undefined","ordered_semantics":["If both truthy: return parentPath+childPath when childPath starts with backslash, otherwise parentPath+backslash+childPath.","Otherwise return whichever path truthy, else undefined."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["No trailing separator normalization, canonicalization, absolute-path handling or traversal filtering."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.convertAscii","inputs":{"bytes":"byte-like array","startPos":"default0","length":"default bytes.length","isCheckPhase6":"default false"},"outputs":"string","ordered_semantics":["Return empty when bytes falsy inside function or startPos+length>bytes.length.","When phase6: inspect12 bytes from original start; if first0xff index in0..9 return empty. If first0xff >9 restrict bytes to first10 of this slice and reset start0/length10. Apply same first-index rule for0x3f using original12-byte slice (even if previous restriction happened). Not-found index -1 does not reject/restrict.","Iterate requested bytes: values outside printable0x20..0x7e except NUL, and doublequote0x22/slash0x2f/backslash0x5c => underscore0x5f. NUL terminates early; append String.fromCharCode otherwise."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["Calling with undefined bytes and omitted length evaluates bytes.length before body and throws; explicit length bypasses that default evaluation. No trim/padding."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.writeRequestSearchInfo","inputs":{},"outputs":"Promise<void>","ordered_semantics":["Generate R_<vin>_<local YYYYMMDDhhmmss>.json and store requestSearchInfoFileName.","PF writeFile({path:mergePath(jsonFilePath,requestSearchInfoFileName),mode:0,data:JSON.stringify(saveRequestSearchInfo)})."],"error_cancel_cleanup":["Write failure swallowed; outer onErrorCommon drops reason; no cancel guard."],"edge_cases":[],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.getSVIParameter","inputs":{},"outputs":"Promise<{requestSearchJsonFileName,searchJsonFileName,reproAutoDriveSystems:Array,vin,uniqueId,isAISAC2:true}>","ordered_semantics":["Collect elm.ecuId for every selectedRowList entry without dedupe/conversion; return as reproAutoDriveSystems.","Return current request/send filenames, vin, receiveDataRequestParam?.requestSearchInfo?.ID, isAISAC2:true."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["File contents are not read or validated here; uniqueId optional."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.setSVIParameter","inputs":{"param.parameter":"{requestSearchJsonFileName,searchJsonFileName,vin,uniqueId}"},"outputs":"Promise<void>","ordered_semantics":["Copy filenames/VIN into initData; replace receiveDataRequestParam with {requestSearchInfo:{ID:uniqueId}}.","Resolve void."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["Does not reconstruct HashValue, softwareId, sendingData, selectedRowList, download state or paths."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.onErrorCommon","inputs":{"model":"unused caught error argument"},"outputs":"rejected Promise<void>","ordered_semantics":["Always Promise.reject() with no reason."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":[],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.makeLocaleTime","inputs":{"plannedOutageTime":"T-delimited date-time string"},"outputs":"string YYYY/M/D H:mm","ordered_semantics":["Split date by dash and time by colon; Number-convert year/month-1/day/hour/minute. Ignore seconds/timezone suffix.","Construct Date(Date.UTC(...)), then format using local year/month/day/hour and two-digit local minute."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["No parsing validation; missing T/time can throw; malformed numbers can format NaN."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"id":"upgrade.worker.exceptDuplexFileInfoList","inputs":{"list":"array of {fileName,...}"},"outputs":"array preserving first exact-name occurrence","ordered_semantics":["Use ordinary {} map; for each fileInfo skip if map[fileName] truthy, else set true and append original object reference."],"error_cancel_cleanup":[],"edge_cases":["Case-sensitive dedupe despite case-insensitive later file checks. Inherited truthy object property names are treated already seen."],"owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/upgrade/upgrade_worker.js"]},
  {"name":"GtsPFApi","member":"js/gts/common/gts_platform_api.js","semantics":"Singleton constructor returns existing instance if object; otherwise stores commonInfo, initializes PF/user languages empty, creates raw interface and ProcessLogger; worker normally uses previously initialized singleton.","id":"FlashingFrontend.upgrade.helper.js/gts/common/gts_platform_api.js::GtsPFApi","owner":"FlashingFrontend","source_ids":["cuw_utility.flash-ui.gts.js/gts/common/gts_platform_api.js"]},
